WEBVTT


00:01:13.169 --> 00:01:13.601
¶ ¶


00:01:20.646 --> 00:01:24.182
- [breathing heavily]


00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:32.122
¶ ¶


00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:17.368
thud!


00:02:40.459 --> 00:02:42.960
[baby crying]


00:03:03.047 --> 00:03:04.382
[pounding on door]


00:03:04.383 --> 00:03:05.549
- LYDIA!


00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.185
OPEN THE DOOR.
LET ME IN!


00:03:08.186 --> 00:03:10.120
[pounding]


00:03:27.472 --> 00:03:30.641
LYDIA, I KNOW
YOU HAVE THE CHILD.


00:03:42.721 --> 00:03:44.722
THEY'RE COMING FOR YOU, LYDIA.


00:03:49.027 --> 00:03:51.128
LYDIA!


00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:53.864
THE PECKS JUST WANT
THEIR BABY.


00:03:53.865 --> 00:03:56.434
[baby crying]


00:04:12.383 --> 00:04:14.618
[choking]


00:04:14.619 --> 00:04:18.455
- [groaning]


00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:32.036
crack!


00:04:32.037 --> 00:04:33.570
AH!


00:04:33.571 --> 00:04:37.341
[breathing heavily]


00:04:38.576 --> 00:04:42.146
[speaking French]


00:04:42.147 --> 00:04:44.915
- [crying]


00:04:44.916 --> 00:04:47.484
[pounding on door]


00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:58.428
- [speaking French]


00:04:58.429 --> 00:05:01.999
- LYDIA!
DON'T!


00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:07.872
PLEASE.


00:05:07.873 --> 00:05:10.775
- [speaking French]


00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:13.744
PARDONNEZ-MOI, MONSIEUR.


00:05:13.745 --> 00:05:15.012
PARDONNEZ-MOI.


00:05:21.853 --> 00:05:27.258
[baby cooing]


00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:28.358
- [screams]


00:05:28.359 --> 00:05:31.728
[gunshot]


00:05:31.729 --> 00:05:34.731
[ominous music]


00:05:34.732 --> 00:05:40.271
¶ ¶


00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:43.808
- [inhales deeply]


00:05:43.809 --> 00:05:45.709
[clamoromh]


00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:47.111
- GIVE ME MY BABY!


00:05:47.112 --> 00:05:48.813
OH, MY SON!


00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:52.749
[screaming]


00:05:58.756 --> 00:06:00.657
[screaming]


00:06:00.658 --> 00:06:03.460
YOU KILLED MY BABY!


00:06:03.461 --> 00:06:05.963
I WANT MY SON!


00:06:13.338 --> 00:06:16.040
[sprawling rock music]


00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:21.411
¶ ¶


00:06:21.412 --> 00:06:24.014
- PICK ANY 13-YEAR PERIOD IN
THE HISTORY OF THE STOCK MARKET,


00:06:24.015 --> 00:06:26.884
AND YOU'LL SEE AN INVESTOR
MADE AT LEAST 10%.


00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:28.319
THE LESSON?


00:06:28.320 --> 00:06:29.920
SLOW AND STEADY WINS THE RACE.


00:06:29.921 --> 00:06:33.290
- BUT DOESN'T THAT INVESTOR HAVE
A RESPONSIBILITY TO BE ACTIVE?


00:06:33.291 --> 00:06:35.492
TAKE ANY OF THOSE
13-YEAR PERIODS


00:06:35.493 --> 00:06:37.127
AND LET ME MAKE ONE TRADE,


00:06:37.128 --> 00:06:38.162
JUST ONE TRADE.


00:06:38.163 --> 00:06:41.165
THEN 10% CAN BECOME
100 OR 1,000.


00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:43.901
- OR IN THAT ONE TRADE,
YOU COULD LOSE IT ALL.


00:06:43.902 --> 00:06:45.269
- IF YOU CAN'T TAKE THE HEAT,


00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:47.504
THEN GET OUT OF THE KITCHEN.


00:06:47.505 --> 00:06:51.008
- JUST LIKE A WOMAN TO COMPARE
INVESTING TO COOKING.


00:06:51.009 --> 00:06:52.176
- [chuckles]


00:06:52.177 --> 00:06:53.643
- OKAY, THAT'S ALL FOR TODAY.


00:06:53.644 --> 00:06:55.412
SEE YOU GUYS NEXT WEEK.


00:07:11.696 --> 00:07:14.064
- JENNY-BOO.


00:07:14.065 --> 00:07:15.499
- HEY.


00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:16.867
- HEY?


00:07:16.868 --> 00:07:19.403
I TOOK THE DAY OFF WORK
IN CELEBRATION OF YOUR BIRTHDAY.


00:07:19.404 --> 00:07:21.138
ALL I GET'S "HEY"?


00:07:21.139 --> 00:07:24.275
- I'M SORRY.
THANK YOU.


00:07:24.276 --> 00:07:26.977
NO, IT'S JUST, SO FAR,


00:07:26.978 --> 00:07:28.512
YOU'RE THE ONLY ONE
WHO'S REMEMBERED.


00:07:28.513 --> 00:07:29.780
- REALLY?
- YES.


00:07:29.781 --> 00:07:31.248
- NAH-AH.


00:07:31.249 --> 00:07:34.118
- ANNETTE HAS AN ENTIRE
FOOTBALL FIELD


00:07:34.119 --> 00:07:35.485
SING HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO HER.


00:07:35.486 --> 00:07:36.753
ME?


00:07:36.754 --> 00:07:40.024
I GET MY BALLS BUSTED BY
PROFESSOR DINGLEBERRY IN THERE.


00:07:40.025 --> 00:07:41.292
- [laughing]
UGH.


00:07:41.293 --> 00:07:42.659
WELL, WHAT ABOUT EVAN?


00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:46.096
- HE'S PROBABLY SLEEPING IT OFF
IN SOME FRAT HOUSE.


00:07:46.097 --> 00:07:47.731
- OR NOT.


00:07:47.732 --> 00:07:50.634
- HAPPY BIRTHDAY,
JENNIFER RITCHIE!


00:07:50.635 --> 00:07:51.969
- I'M OUT OF HERE.
BYE-BYE.


00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:53.770
- HEY, WAIT.
WHAT ABOUT TONIGHT?


00:07:53.771 --> 00:07:55.272
- I'M GONNA TRY
AND MAKE IT.


00:07:55.273 --> 00:07:56.307
- HILLARY.


00:07:56.308 --> 00:07:57.774
- IT'S KEN.


00:07:57.775 --> 00:08:00.044
HE HAS A NEW ROLE-PLAYING
SCENARIO ALL PLANNED OUT,


00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:02.646
WHERE HE'S THE AMERICAN
WOUNDED SOLDIER,


00:08:02.647 --> 00:08:03.914
AND I'M...


00:08:03.915 --> 00:08:05.382
[in French accent]
THE FRENCH NURSE.


00:08:05.383 --> 00:08:06.817
I KNOW, I MEAN,
WHATEVER HAPPENED TO


00:08:06.818 --> 00:08:08.652
[in French accent]
A SIMPLE FINGER IN THE BUTT?


00:08:08.653 --> 00:08:09.653
IT USED TO BE ENOUGH.


00:08:09.654 --> 00:08:10.887
- [laughing]


00:08:10.888 --> 00:08:12.589
EVEN WITH THE ACCENT,
IT'S STILL GROSS.


00:08:12.590 --> 00:08:14.291
- YOU HAVEN'T HAD BOYFRIENDS
WHO LIKE THAT?


00:08:14.292 --> 00:08:15.625
- NO.
- REALLY?


00:08:15.626 --> 00:08:17.294
- NO. NO.


00:08:17.295 --> 00:08:19.096
- OKAY, SO I'M A SLUT, THEN.


00:08:19.097 --> 00:08:20.464
BYE.


00:08:20.465 --> 00:08:22.899
- HAPPY BIRTHDAY.
- HMM.


00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.568
- WHAT'S WRONG?


00:08:24.569 --> 00:08:27.737
- DO YOU THINK
I'M A GOOD FRIEND?


00:08:27.738 --> 00:08:29.906
- YOU'RE AN EXCELLENT FRIEND.


00:08:29.907 --> 00:08:31.208
- THANK YOU.


00:08:31.209 --> 00:08:33.477
I THINK SO.


00:08:33.478 --> 00:08:35.980
I REALLY TRY TO GO OUT OF MY WAY
FOR PEOPLE


00:08:35.981 --> 00:08:38.582
TO MAKE THEM FEEL SPECIAL
ON THEIR BIRTHDAYS.


00:08:38.583 --> 00:08:43.053
HILLARY, I TOOK HER ON
A SHOPPING SPREE TO FOREVER 21.


00:08:43.054 --> 00:08:47.992
ANNETTE, I BAKED HER THAT
RIDICULOUS VEGAN-IZED CAKE.


00:08:47.993 --> 00:08:49.860
I DON'T EVEN--I STILL DON'T EVEN
KNOW WHAT IT IS,


00:08:49.861 --> 00:08:50.927
BUT I DID IT.


00:08:50.928 --> 00:08:52.096
- HEY, WELL, REMEMBER,


00:08:52.097 --> 00:08:53.464
JUST GIVE IT TIME, BABE.


00:08:53.465 --> 00:08:54.564
THE DAY IS STILL YOUNG.


00:08:54.565 --> 00:08:56.000
- YEAH.


00:08:56.001 --> 00:08:57.834
YOU REMEMBERED, RIGHT?


00:08:57.835 --> 00:08:59.836
- WAIT, WHAT ARE WE
TALKING ABOUT?


00:08:59.837 --> 00:09:03.273
OF COURSE I REMEMBERED.
COME ON.


00:09:03.274 --> 00:09:05.075
- OKAY.


00:09:05.076 --> 00:09:06.176
SO WHAT DID YOU GET ME?


00:09:06.177 --> 00:09:07.644
- HMM.
DOESN'T FIT IN MY POCKET.


00:09:07.645 --> 00:09:09.579
GOT TO TAKE YOU TO IT.


00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.348
- GOT TO TAKE ME TO IT?


00:09:11.349 --> 00:09:12.749
- MM-HMM.


00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:14.918
- OKAY.


00:09:14.919 --> 00:09:18.155
WE ARE NOT GOING
TO BURGER KING AGAIN.


00:09:18.156 --> 00:09:20.157
EVAN REYNOLDS,
EVEN AS A JOKE,


00:09:20.158 --> 00:09:22.226
THIS WILL BACKFIRE ON YOU.


00:09:22.227 --> 00:09:25.429
- JENNIFER RITCHIE,
IT'S NOT BURGER KING.


00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:27.998
- OKAY. GOOD.


00:09:27.999 --> 00:09:29.766
THAT'S GOOD.


00:09:29.767 --> 00:09:32.336
SO WHEN DO I GET TO SEE IT?


00:09:32.337 --> 00:09:35.572
- HMM, HOW ABOUT RIGHT NOW?
- YEAH?


00:09:37.875 --> 00:09:39.176
YOU PACKED A BAG?


00:09:39.177 --> 00:09:40.544
- MM-HMM.


00:09:40.545 --> 00:09:43.147
- WE'RE GOING SOMEWHERE?
- MM-HMM.


00:09:43.148 --> 00:09:45.249
- I LOVE IT.


00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:47.751
- COME ON. LET'S GO.
- YES.


00:09:47.752 --> 00:09:49.153
WHERE ARE WE GOING?


00:09:49.154 --> 00:09:50.454
- HMM, DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.


00:09:50.455 --> 00:09:52.523
- [laughing]


00:09:52.524 --> 00:09:54.191
I'LL BE LIKE THAT KID:
"WHERE WE GOING?


00:09:54.192 --> 00:09:58.195
ARE WE THERE YET?
ARE WE THERE YET?"


00:09:58.196 --> 00:10:00.764
[somber piano music]


00:10:00.765 --> 00:10:02.666
I WANT TO OPEN MY EYES.


00:10:02.667 --> 00:10:03.833
- YOU KEEP YOUR EYES CLOSED.


00:10:03.834 --> 00:10:04.834
- I CAN'T.


00:10:04.835 --> 00:10:06.103
I'M STARTING TO GET CARSICK.


00:10:06.104 --> 00:10:08.172
- THERE IS NO SUCH THING
AS GETTING CARSICK.


00:10:08.173 --> 00:10:10.407
IT'S A SCIENTIFIC FACT.


00:10:10.408 --> 00:10:12.909
- FINE, BUT IF I PUKE,
I'M DOING IT ON YOU.


00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.478
SCIENTIFIC FACT.


00:10:14.479 --> 00:10:16.746
- YOU KNOW, SOME PEOPLE ARE INTO
THAT SORT OF THING, YOU KNOW.


00:10:20.118 --> 00:10:21.818
- WAIT A MINUTE.


00:10:21.819 --> 00:10:24.621
ARE YOU TAKING ME
TO A REMOTE LOCATION


00:10:24.622 --> 00:10:27.524
WHERE YOU PLAN ON MURDERING ME
FOR MY BIRTHDAY?


00:10:27.525 --> 00:10:28.725
- DAMN IT.


00:10:28.726 --> 00:10:30.294
SUPPOSED TO BE A SURPRISE.


00:10:30.295 --> 00:10:32.896
- DON'T WORRY.
I'LL ACT SURPRISED.


00:10:32.897 --> 00:10:35.466
[laughing]


00:10:37.068 --> 00:10:38.068
- HEY, NO PEEKING!


00:10:38.069 --> 00:10:39.302
- I'M NOT PEEKING.


00:10:39.303 --> 00:10:40.737
- KEEP 'EM CLOSED.
- WHO WAS PEEKING?


00:10:40.738 --> 00:10:42.405
- DO IT AGAIN.
SEE WHAT HAPPENS.


00:10:42.406 --> 00:10:44.207
ALMOST THERE.
KEEP 'EM CLOSED.


00:10:44.208 --> 00:10:45.442
- WHAT ARE YOU GONNA DO?


00:10:45.443 --> 00:10:47.611
- WELL, I DON'T WANT IT
TO COME TO THIS,


00:10:47.612 --> 00:10:50.013
BUT IF I HAVE TO MAKE YOU
GO DOWN ON ME, I WILL.


00:10:50.014 --> 00:10:51.682
- I WILL BITE IT.


00:10:51.683 --> 00:10:53.684
- [laughs]


00:10:53.685 --> 00:10:56.687
[foreboding orchestral music]


00:10:56.688 --> 00:11:04.628
¶ ¶


00:11:06.965 --> 00:11:08.498
- WE'RE HERE?


00:11:08.499 --> 00:11:10.767
- YOU READY?
- YES.


00:11:10.768 --> 00:11:12.836
- OKAY.
YOU CAN OPEN THEM.


00:11:17.341 --> 00:11:19.209
IT'S A HOUSE.


00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.878
- YEP.
WHAT THE FUCK?


00:11:21.879 --> 00:11:23.213
- JENNY, WHAT?


00:11:23.214 --> 00:11:25.482
- NO, IS THIS--


00:11:25.483 --> 00:11:27.250
IS THIS A JOKE?


00:11:27.251 --> 00:11:29.920
- NO, IT'S NOT A JOKE.


00:11:32.991 --> 00:11:35.692
- DID YOU THINK THAT I WOULD
THINK THIS IS FUNNY?


00:11:35.693 --> 00:11:37.193
- IT'S NOT SUPPOSED TO BE--


00:11:37.194 --> 00:11:39.029
- BRINGING ME TO A HAUNTED HOUSE
ON MY BIRTHDAY.


00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:40.063
- IT'S NOT A HAUNTED HOUSE.


00:11:40.064 --> 00:11:41.264
IT'S NOT SUPPOSED
TO BE FUNNY.


00:11:41.265 --> 00:11:44.434
- TAKE ME HOME.


00:11:44.435 --> 00:11:45.736
- THIS IS HOME.


00:11:45.737 --> 00:11:48.605
- WHAT?


00:11:48.606 --> 00:11:51.041
- I BOUGHT THIS PLACE...


00:11:51.042 --> 00:11:53.143
FOR US.


00:12:18.602 --> 00:12:21.672
- HAVE YOU LOST YOUR MIND?


00:12:21.673 --> 00:12:23.674
WHAT ABOUT OUR APARTMENT?


00:12:23.675 --> 00:12:26.643
WHAT ABOUT SCHOOL?


00:12:26.644 --> 00:12:28.679
THIS IS SO FRICKIN' YOU.


00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:29.946
- WHAT DO YOU MEAN IT'S ME?


00:12:29.947 --> 00:12:32.315
- ALWAYS BOUNCING AROUND
FROM ONE THING TO ANOTHER:


00:12:32.316 --> 00:12:33.917
CHANGING JOBS,
CHANGING MAJORS,


00:12:33.918 --> 00:12:35.952
MOVING EVERY SEMESTER.


00:12:35.953 --> 00:12:38.055
WE SHOULD BE INTERNING
THIS SUMMER, EVAN,


00:12:38.056 --> 00:12:39.189
LOOKING FOR A JOB,


00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:40.691
NOT OUT
IN THE MIDDLE OF NOWHERE


00:12:40.692 --> 00:12:45.062
ON SOME CRAZY
REAL ESTATE SPECULATION.


00:12:45.063 --> 00:12:46.963
LOOK AT THIS PLACE.
IT IS TRASH.


00:12:46.964 --> 00:12:49.099
- LET'S GET MARRIED,
ALL RIGHT?


00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.967
NO, NO, WAIT.
I NEED MY SPACE.


00:12:50.968 --> 00:12:52.569
NO, NO, NO.
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.


00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:53.704
WE SHOULD SEE OTHER PEOPLE.


00:12:53.705 --> 00:12:55.572
NO, WAIT!
WAIT, I MISS YOU.


00:12:55.573 --> 00:12:56.740
LET'S GET BACK TOGETHER.


00:12:56.741 --> 00:12:58.541
- WHAT THE HELL
DOES THAT MEAN?


00:12:58.542 --> 00:13:01.444
- IT MEANS I'M NOT THE ONLY ONE
THAT'S BOUNCING AROUND.


00:13:07.752 --> 00:13:09.853
OPEN IT.


00:13:21.966 --> 00:13:24.735
- "TO THE LOVE OF MY LIFE,


00:13:24.736 --> 00:13:27.370
"THE ONE THAT I WANT TO BE
MY WIFE.


00:13:27.371 --> 00:13:29.372
"I KNOW IT DOESN'T LOOK
LIKE MUCH,


00:13:29.373 --> 00:13:32.709
"BUT I HAVE
AN EXTRAORDINARY HUNCH


00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:34.244
"THAT IF WE FIX THIS UP,


00:13:34.245 --> 00:13:37.781
"WITH ANY LUCK, WE'LL SELL IT
FOR A MILLION BUCKS.


00:13:37.782 --> 00:13:40.617
THEN WE CAN RETIRE
AND HAVE SEX ALL THE TIME."


00:13:40.618 --> 00:13:41.752
REALLY?


00:13:41.753 --> 00:13:43.186
- I KNOW THAT LAST LINE
DIDN'T RHYME,


00:13:43.187 --> 00:13:45.155
BUT IT CAME FROM THE HEART.


00:13:51.729 --> 00:13:55.899
THERE'S ANOTHER PIECE OF PAPER
IN THERE.


00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.603
- YOU SIGNED MY NAME?


00:14:00.604 --> 00:14:03.940
- YOU ARE A HOMEOWNER.


00:14:03.941 --> 00:14:08.378
- I AM A HOMEOWNER.


00:14:08.379 --> 00:14:09.612
- IT'S A PROPERTY INVESTMENT.


00:14:09.613 --> 00:14:11.648
I'VE BEEN LOOKING EVERY DAY
SINCE DECEMBER,


00:14:11.649 --> 00:14:13.116
AND I FOUND IT ONLINE.


00:14:13.117 --> 00:14:16.153
SO I DROVE UP HERE, AND I MADE
AN OFFER THAT DAY.


00:14:16.154 --> 00:14:17.988
AND, LOOK, I KNOW IT'S NOT
YOUR DREAM HOUSE,


00:14:17.989 --> 00:14:21.357
BUT IT'S BIG,


00:14:21.358 --> 00:14:25.328
AND IT COMES
WITH A LOT OF LAND.


00:14:25.329 --> 00:14:27.430
- HOW MUCH LAND?
- 40 ACRES.


00:14:27.431 --> 00:14:28.598
- WOW.


00:14:28.599 --> 00:14:30.267
- I ASKED THEM IF THEY COULD
THROW IN A MULE,


00:14:30.268 --> 00:14:31.835
BUT NO DICE.


00:14:31.836 --> 00:14:33.670
- NO DICE.


00:14:33.671 --> 00:14:34.671
- IF WE MARKET IT RIGHT,


00:14:34.672 --> 00:14:36.406
WE COULD FLIP THIS HOUSE,


00:14:36.407 --> 00:14:37.640
AND WE COULD MAKE
A LOT OF MONEY:


00:14:37.641 --> 00:14:40.310
PAY OFF OUR STUDENT LOANS,


00:14:40.311 --> 00:14:45.481
AND WE COULD DO THE WEDDING
IN HAWAII.


00:14:45.482 --> 00:14:47.784
- I WAS HOPING FOR A RING.


00:14:47.785 --> 00:14:49.752
I WAS.


00:14:49.753 --> 00:14:54.024
BUT THIS IS VERY ROMANTIC


00:14:54.025 --> 00:14:56.592
IN A VERY WEIRD KIND OF WAY.


00:14:56.593 --> 00:15:00.230
- EXACTLY WHAT I WAS HOPING
YOU WERE GOING TO SAY.


00:15:00.231 --> 00:15:01.531
- OH...


00:15:01.532 --> 00:15:03.733
I HAVE TO CALL HILLARY.
OH, MY GOODNESS.


00:15:03.734 --> 00:15:04.868
TELL HER WE GOT A HOUSE.


00:15:04.869 --> 00:15:06.436
- [laughs]


00:15:06.437 --> 00:15:08.805
OH, THAT'S THE ONE THING:


00:15:08.806 --> 00:15:10.907
SHITTY CELL SERVICE.


00:15:10.908 --> 00:15:13.276
- YEAH, SEE, I KNEW IT WAS
TOO GOOD TO BE TRUE.


00:15:13.277 --> 00:15:14.811
- HEY, STOP IT!
- I'M OUT!


00:15:14.812 --> 00:15:18.381
[laughing]


00:15:19.616 --> 00:15:21.818
- WHAT DID YOU PAY
FOR THIS PLACE?


00:15:21.819 --> 00:15:24.921
- 10 GRAND.
- 10 GRAND.


00:15:24.922 --> 00:15:26.489
- EVERYTHING IN MY SAVINGS.


00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:28.291
- THAT'S, LIKE, FREE.


00:15:28.292 --> 00:15:29.559
WHY?


00:15:29.560 --> 00:15:31.627
- BECAUSE THIS IS
THE MIDDLE OF NOWHERE,


00:15:31.628 --> 00:15:33.429
AND NO ONE ELSE WANTS TO BE
OUT HERE.


00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:35.031
- [laughing]


00:15:35.032 --> 00:15:38.468
I'M SORRY I WAS SUCH A BITCH.
I'M SORRY.


00:15:38.469 --> 00:15:41.004
I'VE JUST BEEN STRESSED OUT
AND...


00:15:41.005 --> 00:15:43.506
- HEY, IT'S OKAY.
AT LEAST WE HAVE EACH OTHER.


00:15:43.507 --> 00:15:45.208
- THAT BETTER BE ENOUGH,


00:15:45.209 --> 00:15:47.077
BECAUSE WITH A HOUSE
IN BUMFUCK, EGYPT,


00:15:47.078 --> 00:15:49.045
WE REALLY DON'T HAVE
MUCH CHOICE.


00:15:49.046 --> 00:15:51.114
- JUST WAIT UNTIL YOU SEE
THE REST OF IT.


00:15:51.115 --> 00:15:53.483
DON'T MESS WITH A GUY
THAT'S IN LOVE, ALL RIGHT?


00:15:53.484 --> 00:15:55.551
- [laughs]


00:15:55.552 --> 00:15:58.554
[ominous music]


00:15:58.555 --> 00:16:01.391
¶ ¶


00:16:01.392 --> 00:16:03.793
[clamoring]
GOT IT?


00:16:03.794 --> 00:16:06.930
WOW.
LOOK AT THIS PLACE.


00:16:06.931 --> 00:16:08.765
THIS IS EXCITING, BABE.


00:16:08.766 --> 00:16:10.333
- YEAH.


00:16:13.404 --> 00:16:14.470
YEAH.


00:16:14.471 --> 00:16:15.638
- I'M READY.


00:16:15.639 --> 00:16:17.707
- HOPEFULLY OUR KEY'S
GOING TO WORK.


00:16:22.346 --> 00:16:24.314
- OOH.


00:16:24.315 --> 00:16:26.682
THAT'S AN INTERESTING SMELL.


00:16:26.683 --> 00:16:28.318
- SMELLS LIKE
YOUR BELLY BUTTON.


00:16:28.319 --> 00:16:32.488
- [laughing]


00:16:32.489 --> 00:16:34.657
THAT IS JUST SEXY.


00:16:34.658 --> 00:16:38.028
- LET'S GET SOME LIGHTS.


00:16:38.029 --> 00:16:39.562
DAMN.


00:16:39.563 --> 00:16:40.964
I CALLED TO GET
THE POWER TURNED ON,


00:16:40.965 --> 00:16:42.698
BUT I GUESS
THEY NEVER MADE IT.


00:16:42.699 --> 00:16:45.068
- WHAT?
NO SOLAR PANELS?


00:16:45.069 --> 00:16:47.337
NOT VERY GREEN OF YOU.


00:16:47.338 --> 00:16:49.639
[flicking light switch]


00:16:49.640 --> 00:16:53.576
- DAMN.


00:16:53.577 --> 00:16:55.778
[flicking light switch]


00:16:55.779 --> 00:16:57.914
WE GOT PLATES.


00:16:57.915 --> 00:17:01.952
- NO, EVAN.
THIS IS ANTIQUE CHINA.


00:17:01.953 --> 00:17:04.854
THIS IS REAL SILVER.


00:17:04.855 --> 00:17:07.190
LIKE, WHY WOULD THEY LEAVE
THIS STUFF BEHIND?


00:17:07.191 --> 00:17:10.827
IT'S, LIKE, GOT TO BE
FAMILY HEIRLOOMS OR SOMETHING.


00:17:10.828 --> 00:17:12.996
- THE CONTRACT SAID WE GET
ALL THE FURNISHINGS.


00:17:12.997 --> 00:17:15.832
- REALLY?


00:17:15.833 --> 00:17:18.234
[laughing]


00:17:19.303 --> 00:17:21.804
THIS PLACE IS INCREDIBLE.


00:17:21.805 --> 00:17:23.073
- RIGHT?


00:17:23.074 --> 00:17:25.608
- THE DOWNSTAIRS IS BIGGER
THAN OUR APARTMENT.


00:17:25.609 --> 00:17:28.544
- WAIT FOR IT.
WAIT FOR IT.


00:17:28.545 --> 00:17:30.813
- OH.


00:17:30.814 --> 00:17:34.217
THIS STOVE IS AMAZING.


00:17:34.218 --> 00:17:35.685
- I KNEW YOU'D LOVE THAT THING.


00:17:35.686 --> 00:17:39.489
- OH, I THINK I ACTUALLY SAW
SOME POTS AND PANS.


00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:41.524
- YEAH, THERE SHOULD BE
EVERYTHING THAT WE NEED HERE,


00:17:41.525 --> 00:17:42.525
PRETTY MUCH.


00:17:42.526 --> 00:17:43.526
IT CAME PRETTY LOADED.


00:17:43.527 --> 00:17:44.794
- THERE THEY ARE.


00:17:44.795 --> 00:17:49.599
- ALL RIGHT, GIRL.
I KNEW YOU'D FIND THEM.


00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:51.567
HEY, REMEMBER,
IF YOU FIND AN OLD TWINKIE,


00:17:51.568 --> 00:17:53.103
IT'S STILL GOOD.


00:17:53.104 --> 00:17:55.571
- [laughing]
THAT'S REALLY GROSS.


00:17:59.110 --> 00:18:01.111
LOOK, BABE.


00:18:01.112 --> 00:18:02.545
WE GOT RUNNING WATER.


00:18:02.546 --> 00:18:04.047
WATER COMPANY MUST HAVE COME.


00:18:04.048 --> 00:18:05.148
- HMM.


00:18:05.149 --> 00:18:06.782
BUT IT'S RUN
ON AN ELECTRIC WELL.


00:18:06.783 --> 00:18:08.251
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?


00:18:08.252 --> 00:18:11.821
HEY, HOLD ON A SECOND.
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.


00:18:20.898 --> 00:18:24.166
HMM.


00:18:28.238 --> 00:18:31.240
[tense music]


00:18:31.241 --> 00:18:37.547
¶ ¶


00:18:37.548 --> 00:18:39.148
WHAT THE HELL?


00:18:46.824 --> 00:18:48.658
WHAT THE HECK IS THIS?


00:18:48.659 --> 00:18:56.599
¶ ¶


00:19:07.812 --> 00:19:09.646
HUH.


00:19:12.716 --> 00:19:13.716
- EASY, KID.


00:19:13.717 --> 00:19:14.717
rip!


00:19:14.718 --> 00:19:15.718
- FUCK!


00:19:15.719 --> 00:19:17.119
- DAMN!


00:19:17.120 --> 00:19:18.955
SCRAPPY LITTLE
SON OF A BITCH.


00:19:18.956 --> 00:19:22.492
- [breathing heavily]


00:19:24.562 --> 00:19:26.062
WHAT THE FUCK'S
YOUR PROBLEM, MAN?


00:19:26.063 --> 00:19:27.997
- HEY.


00:19:34.705 --> 00:19:38.608
YOU'RE ONE OF THEM
SENSITIVE BOYS, AIN'T YA?


00:19:38.609 --> 00:19:41.043
AIN'T A THING
TO BE ASHAMED OF.


00:19:41.044 --> 00:19:45.448
A LOT OF PEOPLE LIKE THAT.


00:19:45.449 --> 00:19:47.083
YOU KNOW I'M HERE
TO TURN YOU ON, RIGHT?


00:19:47.084 --> 00:19:48.084
- WHAT?


00:19:48.085 --> 00:19:50.219
- YOUR POWER.


00:19:50.220 --> 00:19:53.890
WANT YOUR HOUSE TO BURN DOWN?


00:19:55.258 --> 00:19:56.993
- THE BREAKER BOX IS OVER THERE.


00:19:56.994 --> 00:19:58.862
- I'LL TAKE CARE OF YA.


00:19:58.863 --> 00:20:01.364
I'LL TAKE CARE OF YA GOOD.


00:20:04.768 --> 00:20:08.671
- AH.


00:20:08.672 --> 00:20:10.907
OW.


00:20:15.445 --> 00:20:17.514
WHAT THE HELL?


00:20:23.854 --> 00:20:26.055
IS THIS NATIVE AMERICAN?


00:20:29.593 --> 00:20:30.560
[grunts]


00:20:36.266 --> 00:20:38.001
OH, SHIT!


00:20:38.002 --> 00:20:39.268
UGH!


00:20:43.507 --> 00:20:44.507
[sniffing]


00:20:44.508 --> 00:20:47.877
[groans]


00:20:47.878 --> 00:20:50.880
[eerie music]


00:20:50.881 --> 00:20:53.115
¶ ¶


00:20:53.116 --> 00:20:54.851
COOL.


00:20:54.852 --> 00:21:02.792
¶ ¶


00:21:27.885 --> 00:21:29.285
- OH, YEAH.


00:21:36.026 --> 00:21:38.327
THAT'S MY GIRL.


00:21:42.399 --> 00:21:43.666
THERE WE GO.


00:21:47.938 --> 00:21:50.940
[anxious music]


00:21:50.941 --> 00:21:58.414
¶ ¶


00:21:58.415 --> 00:21:59.882
[buzzing]


00:22:09.994 --> 00:22:11.094
- OH!


00:22:11.095 --> 00:22:12.561
- WHOA!


00:22:12.562 --> 00:22:14.196
- OH, GOD!


00:22:14.197 --> 00:22:17.700
DON'T SNEAK UP ON ME
LIKE THAT.


00:22:17.701 --> 00:22:20.202
- OH, SHIT!


00:22:20.203 --> 00:22:21.938
THAT IS SO DISGUSTING.


00:22:21.939 --> 00:22:23.973
OH, IS THAT PINEAPPLE?


00:22:23.974 --> 00:22:25.008
I FUCKING HATE PINEAPPLE.


00:22:25.009 --> 00:22:26.308
- GET IT OUT OF HERE.


00:22:26.309 --> 00:22:27.877
- I THOUGHT THE KITCHEN
WAS YOUR DOMAIN.


00:22:27.878 --> 00:22:28.978
- EVAN REYNOLDS,


00:22:28.979 --> 00:22:30.412
IF YOU EVER WANT
TO SPEAK TO ME AGAIN,


00:22:30.413 --> 00:22:33.315
YOU WILL GET THAT THING
OUT OF HERE.


00:22:33.316 --> 00:22:35.351
- OKAY.


00:22:38.421 --> 00:22:40.023
[groaning]


00:22:40.024 --> 00:22:42.591
OKAY.
ALL RIGHT.


00:22:42.592 --> 00:22:43.960
COME ON, PORKY.


00:22:43.961 --> 00:22:46.428
LET'S GET YOU LORD OF THE FLIES
TO TAKE THE REST ON.


00:22:46.429 --> 00:22:48.464
[exhales deeply]


00:22:48.465 --> 00:22:49.766
- GO!
- I'M GOING.


00:22:49.767 --> 00:22:51.834
- UGH.


00:23:05.549 --> 00:23:07.383
[laughter]


00:23:07.384 --> 00:23:09.618
- UNLESS I'M MISTAKEN,


00:23:09.619 --> 00:23:10.920
I THINK IT'S BEER 30.


00:23:10.921 --> 00:23:15.224
- THAT SOUNDS GOOD.


00:23:15.225 --> 00:23:17.426
WHERE ARE WE STAYING
TONIGHT?


00:23:17.427 --> 00:23:18.627
- I BROUGHT THE CAMPING GEAR.


00:23:18.628 --> 00:23:22.231
- SEE, I WAS KIND OF THINKING
ABOUT THAT HOTEL


00:23:22.232 --> 00:23:23.432
OFF THE INTERSTATE...


00:23:23.433 --> 00:23:24.967
- THE ONE THAT'S, LIKE,
AN HOUR AWAY?


00:23:24.968 --> 00:23:27.436
- YEAH.
- COME ON.


00:23:27.437 --> 00:23:29.005
WE GOT TO STAY HERE
SOONER OR LATER.


00:23:29.006 --> 00:23:30.006
IT'LL BE FUN.


00:23:30.007 --> 00:23:32.508
- FUN?
- YES, FUN.


00:23:32.509 --> 00:23:34.744
YOU REMEMBER
WHAT FUN IS, RIGHT?


00:23:34.745 --> 00:23:37.479
- YEAH, I REMEMBER
WHAT FUN IS.


00:23:37.480 --> 00:23:38.715
YES.


00:23:38.716 --> 00:23:40.416
I LIKE FUN.
- YEAH?


00:23:40.417 --> 00:23:44.020
- YES, I LIKE FUN.


00:23:44.021 --> 00:23:46.322
- I KNEW YOU DID.


00:23:47.725 --> 00:23:50.727
[eerie orchestral music]


00:23:50.728 --> 00:23:56.733
¶ ¶


00:23:56.734 --> 00:24:00.002
[crickets chirping]


00:24:04.074 --> 00:24:07.009
[creaking]


00:24:22.860 --> 00:24:24.426
bang!


00:24:30.500 --> 00:24:32.501
- HEY.


00:24:32.502 --> 00:24:34.070
DID YOU HEAR THAT?


00:24:34.071 --> 00:24:38.741
- [mumbling] I DON'T KNOW.
NO.


00:24:38.742 --> 00:24:41.744
[ominous music]


00:24:41.745 --> 00:24:49.685
¶ ¶


00:25:10.240 --> 00:25:15.845
- [heavy breathing]


00:25:15.846 --> 00:25:23.786
¶ ¶


00:25:25.155 --> 00:25:27.957
- [giggling]


00:25:32.029 --> 00:25:33.395
- MARY, WHAT DID I TELL YOU


00:25:33.396 --> 00:25:35.564
ABOUT STAYING AWAY
FROM THAT BOY?


00:25:35.565 --> 00:25:37.633
- I WAS JUST--
- YOU WERE NOTHING.


00:25:37.634 --> 00:25:43.139
NOW GET OUT OF HERE
BEFORE I TELL YOUR MAMA.


00:25:43.140 --> 00:25:45.274
I'M GONNA COUNT TO THREE,


00:25:45.275 --> 00:25:50.412
AND THEN I'M GONNA MAKE YOU WISH
YOU WERE NEVER BORN.


00:25:50.413 --> 00:25:52.148
ONE...


00:25:52.149 --> 00:25:53.349
TWO...


00:25:59.589 --> 00:26:07.529
¶ ¶


00:26:23.013 --> 00:26:24.347
- WHERE DID YOU GO?


00:26:24.348 --> 00:26:26.883
- I HAD TO TAKE CARE
OF SOME BURGLARS.


00:26:26.884 --> 00:26:29.352
- HMM.
THANKS, HONEY.


00:26:29.353 --> 00:26:31.254
- YOU'RE WELCOME.


00:26:37.327 --> 00:26:40.329
[jovial banjo music]


00:26:40.330 --> 00:26:46.535
¶ ¶


00:26:46.536 --> 00:26:47.870
- OOH.


00:26:47.871 --> 00:26:49.906
- [laughing]


00:26:49.907 --> 00:26:52.375
OOH!


00:26:52.376 --> 00:26:54.076
- WHAT THE HELL IS THIS?


00:26:54.077 --> 00:26:58.381
- IT'S AN OLD-FASHIONED
IDIOT DETECTOR.


00:26:58.382 --> 00:27:01.951
AND LOOK--
IT'S WORKING.


00:27:01.952 --> 00:27:03.485
- I DON'T GET IT.


00:27:03.486 --> 00:27:05.254
- THAT'S 'CAUSE
YOU'RE AN IDIOT.


00:27:05.255 --> 00:27:06.255
- OH.


00:27:06.256 --> 00:27:07.556
squeak!


00:27:10.294 --> 00:27:12.494
- CAN I HELP YOU FOLKS
FIND ANYTHING?


00:27:12.495 --> 00:27:14.430
- AH, YEAH.
WE'RE ACTUALLY--


00:27:14.431 --> 00:27:16.832
DO YOU HAVE ANY PAINT
AND DROP CLOTHS, BY ANY CHANCE?


00:27:16.833 --> 00:27:17.967
- I SURE DO.


00:27:17.968 --> 00:27:19.402
I'VE GOT SOME COLOR CHARTS
UP FRONT.


00:27:19.403 --> 00:27:21.203
LET'S GO TAKE A LOOK.
- OKAY.


00:27:34.017 --> 00:27:35.884
- I'M FRED.


00:27:35.885 --> 00:27:37.553
- JENNIFER, EVAN.


00:27:37.554 --> 00:27:39.388
- YOU'RE DOING SOME REMODELING.


00:27:39.389 --> 00:27:41.290
- WE JUST BOUGHT THE OLD
TUCKER PLACE UP THE ROAD.


00:27:41.291 --> 00:27:43.392
WE'RE GONNA BE FIXING IT UP.


00:27:46.129 --> 00:27:47.930
- IT'S A GRAND HOUSE.


00:27:47.931 --> 00:27:49.598
- GRAND, MY ASS.


00:27:49.599 --> 00:27:51.567
- WE CALL HIM MR. PECK.


00:27:51.568 --> 00:27:55.371
- SURPRISED IT'S STILL STANDING
AFTER 50 YEARS.


00:27:55.372 --> 00:27:57.406
- IT'S ACTUALLY
IN PRETTY GOOD SHAPE.


00:27:57.407 --> 00:27:58.407
- YOU DON'T SAY?


00:27:58.408 --> 00:28:00.142
- TUCKERS DIED IN '61.


00:28:00.143 --> 00:28:02.144
THE PLACE HAS BEEN ABANDONED
EVER SINCE.


00:28:02.145 --> 00:28:03.612
- ACTUALLY, DO YOU KNOW WHY


00:28:03.613 --> 00:28:06.248
THEIR FAMILIES NEVER CLAIMED
THEIR THINGS?


00:28:06.249 --> 00:28:09.251
- WELL, THERE WASN'T
ANY FAMILY LEFT.


00:28:09.252 --> 00:28:11.720
THE ESTATE,
IT DIED WHEN THEY DID.


00:28:11.721 --> 00:28:13.122
- HOW'D THEY GO?


00:28:13.123 --> 00:28:15.124
- THEY DIDN'T TELL YOU
AT THE ASSESSOR'S OFFICE?


00:28:15.125 --> 00:28:17.159
- THINK THEY'D HAVE BOUGHT
THE PLACE IF THEY DID?


00:28:17.160 --> 00:28:20.162
- GIVE IT A REST!


00:28:20.163 --> 00:28:22.298
I'M SORRY.


00:28:22.299 --> 00:28:24.000
- WHAT'S THAT ABOUT?


00:28:24.001 --> 00:28:28.170
- LOOK, MISTER, IT'S NOT
MY PLACE TO TALK ABOUT IT.


00:28:28.171 --> 00:28:29.438
I AIN'T SAYING.


00:28:29.439 --> 00:28:31.207
- JUST DON'T GO DIGGING
IN THE BACKYARD.


00:28:31.208 --> 00:28:32.975
THAT'S ALL YOU NEED TO KNOW.


00:28:32.976 --> 00:28:35.077
- WHY?


00:28:36.246 --> 00:28:39.982
- OKAY, UM,
LEMON YELLOW.


00:28:39.983 --> 00:28:43.219
- WHAT?
- YES. LEMON YELLOW.


00:28:43.220 --> 00:28:44.920
THAT'S WHAT I'D LIKE TO PAINT
MY KITCHEN.


00:28:44.921 --> 00:28:46.088
WHAT DO YOU THINK?


00:28:46.089 --> 00:28:47.556
- WITH A LITTLE SEMIGLOSS
WHITE TRIM,


00:28:47.557 --> 00:28:49.492
YOU'LL HAVE A BEAUTIFUL KITCHEN
IS WHAT I THINK.


00:28:49.493 --> 00:28:51.260
AND I'LL DIG UP A COUPLE GALLONS
OF THE STUFF,


00:28:51.261 --> 00:28:52.428
AND I'LL BRING IT BY TOMORROW.


00:28:52.429 --> 00:28:53.429
- THANK YOU.


00:28:53.430 --> 00:28:55.064
COME ON.


00:28:55.065 --> 00:28:56.565
THANK YOU.


00:28:56.566 --> 00:28:59.068
- I REALLY HOPE YOU KIDS BRING
SOME LIGHT BACK TO THAT HOUSE.


00:28:59.069 --> 00:29:02.704
IT'S HAD A DARK CLOUD OVER IT
FOR A LONG TIME.


00:29:02.705 --> 00:29:04.706
squeak!
- WE'LL TRY.


00:29:04.707 --> 00:29:06.509
- PUT THAT DOWN.


00:29:12.115 --> 00:29:13.815
[bells chime]


00:29:13.816 --> 00:29:16.652
- LET ME KNOW WHEN...


00:29:16.653 --> 00:29:18.220
WHEN YOU FIND THOSE PAINTS.


00:29:18.221 --> 00:29:19.355
I'LL TAKE IT OVER.


00:29:19.356 --> 00:29:21.090
- WHY WOULD YOU WANT TO DO THAT
TO YOURSELF?


00:29:21.091 --> 00:29:22.991
- I WANT TO MAKE SURE WHAT WAS
BURIED STAYS BURIED.


00:29:22.992 --> 00:29:24.026
- [inhales deeply]


00:29:24.027 --> 00:29:25.961
[tense music]


00:29:25.962 --> 00:29:28.497
- DIE!


00:29:28.498 --> 00:29:32.068
- PEOPLE DON'T COME BACK
FROM THE DEAD.


00:29:32.069 --> 00:29:34.437
- I WANT TO MAKE SURE.


00:29:37.441 --> 00:29:39.808
- HEY, SAY THAT AGAIN.
I'M STARTING TO LOSE YOU.


00:29:39.809 --> 00:29:42.344
OKAY, GREAT.
THANK YOU, MR. BROWN.


00:29:42.345 --> 00:29:44.046
ALL RIGHT, I'LL--


00:29:44.047 --> 00:29:45.714
HELLO?


00:29:45.715 --> 00:29:49.017
HELLO?
ARE YOU STILL THERE?


00:29:49.018 --> 00:29:51.220
GOD DAMN IT.
LOST HIM.


00:29:51.221 --> 00:29:52.354
- WHO WAS THAT?


00:29:52.355 --> 00:29:53.722
- THAT ANTIQUE COLLECTOR.


00:29:53.723 --> 00:29:54.890
HE'S GONNA COME BY TOMORROW


00:29:54.891 --> 00:29:56.358
TO APPRAISE
EVERYTHING IN THE HOUSE.


00:29:56.359 --> 00:29:57.593
HE SAID
SOME OF THOSE HEIRLOOMS


00:29:57.594 --> 00:30:00.496
COULD BE WORTH
MORE THAN THE PROPERTY ITSELF.


00:30:00.497 --> 00:30:03.499
[ominous orchestral music]


00:30:03.500 --> 00:30:11.440
¶ ¶


00:30:13.410 --> 00:30:15.478
I STILL CAN'T GET OVER
THAT OLD KOOK.


00:30:15.479 --> 00:30:18.447
- WHAT DO YOU THINK
HE WAS TALKING ABOUT?


00:30:18.448 --> 00:30:21.217
- I BET HE WAS JUST PISSED
THAT WE BEAT HIM TO THE PUNCH.


00:30:21.218 --> 00:30:23.285
HE'S PROBABLY IN THE PROCESS
OF COUNTING HIS PENNIES


00:30:23.286 --> 00:30:25.421
BEFORE I SWOOPED IN AND
SNATCHED IT OUT FROM UNDER HIM.


00:30:25.422 --> 00:30:27.089
- [laughing]
LUCKY ME.


00:30:27.090 --> 00:30:30.526
I GOT MY OWN DONALD TRUMP
SITTING RIGHT NEXT TO ME.


00:30:30.527 --> 00:30:31.860
- AT LEAST WE HAVE
OUR FRIENDS HERE


00:30:31.861 --> 00:30:33.429
IN CASE HE TURNS OUT TO BE
A TOTAL NUTJOB.


00:30:33.430 --> 00:30:34.830
- WHAT FRIENDS?


00:30:34.831 --> 00:30:37.399
- FEAST YOUR EYES,
BIRTHDAY GIRL.


00:30:37.400 --> 00:30:38.967
- AH!
[laughing]


00:30:38.968 --> 00:30:41.970
[upbeat rock music]


00:30:41.971 --> 00:30:49.578
¶ ¶


00:30:49.579 --> 00:30:53.815
- HAPPY FUCKING BIRTHDAY,
SUPER CUNT.


00:30:53.816 --> 00:30:54.983
- NICE WORK.


00:30:54.984 --> 00:30:57.419
- HI.


00:30:57.420 --> 00:30:59.655
WHAT ARE YOU GUYS DOING HERE?


00:30:59.656 --> 00:31:00.956
- YOU LIKE THIS?
- I LOVE IT, MAN.


00:31:00.957 --> 00:31:02.291
I'M GONNA BE OUT HERE
ALL THE TIME.


00:31:02.292 --> 00:31:03.992
- WHAT DOWN PAYMENT
DID YOU PUT DOWN ON THIS?


00:31:03.993 --> 00:31:05.327
20%? 10%?


00:31:05.328 --> 00:31:07.095
- I THOUGHT YOU, LIKE,
HATED ME OR SOMETHING.


00:31:07.096 --> 00:31:08.364
- EVAN MADE US PROMISE.


00:31:08.365 --> 00:31:09.765
HE WANTED IT TO BE
REALLY SPECIAL.


00:31:09.766 --> 00:31:12.334
- YOU DID LOOK SO SAD YESTERDAY,
AND I FELT TERRIBLE.


00:31:12.335 --> 00:31:14.336
I WAS GONNA TELL YOU
IF YOU STARTED CRYING.


00:31:14.337 --> 00:31:15.437
- THAT'S VERY SWEET OF YOU.


00:31:15.438 --> 00:31:17.239
- SO THIS IS IT, HUH?
- YEAH.


00:31:17.240 --> 00:31:18.541
- IT'S REALLY CUTE.


00:31:18.542 --> 00:31:20.609
IT'S, LIKE,
BED AND BREAKFASTY.


00:31:20.610 --> 00:31:22.478
- FOR THE MANSON FAMILY.


00:31:22.479 --> 00:31:24.746
- YOU'RE SUCH A BITCH.


00:31:24.747 --> 00:31:27.483
HEY, GUYS.
WHERE YOU GOING?


00:31:27.484 --> 00:31:29.117
- AH, WE'RE GOING OVER
TO THE GRAVEYARD.


00:31:29.118 --> 00:31:30.252
- THE GRAVEYARD?


00:31:30.253 --> 00:31:31.654
THAT'S SO CREEPY.


00:31:31.655 --> 00:31:32.988
- TOTALLY.


00:31:32.989 --> 00:31:35.057
- OKAY, LET ME SHOW YOU
THE REST OF THE HOUSE.


00:31:35.058 --> 00:31:36.758
YOU WILL NOT BELIEVE
WHAT THEY LEFT BEHIND.


00:31:36.759 --> 00:31:38.360
- DID THEY TELL YOU
HOW MANY ACRES THIS IS?


00:31:38.361 --> 00:31:40.396
- IT'S ABOUT 40
GOING THAT WAY.


00:31:40.397 --> 00:31:42.331
- DUDE, YOU SHOULD SET UP
A SHELTER


00:31:42.332 --> 00:31:43.566
FOR AGRICULTURAL RENTALS--


00:31:43.567 --> 00:31:45.901
WRITE THE WHOLE PLACE OFF.


00:31:45.902 --> 00:31:47.469
WHAT?
I STUDIED.


00:31:47.470 --> 00:31:49.037
- IT'S NOT THAT MUCH
TO WRITE OFF, BUDDY.


00:31:49.038 --> 00:31:50.406
I APPRECIATE IT.


00:31:50.407 --> 00:31:52.374
- NOT EVERYTHING'S
AN INVESTMENT OPPORTUNITY.


00:31:52.375 --> 00:31:54.843
- I MEAN, HAVE YOU EVEN BEEN
ON A REAL VACATION?


00:31:54.844 --> 00:31:57.580
- YEAH, THERE WAS THAT YOUNG
LEADERSHIP CONFERENCE IN BURMA.


00:31:57.581 --> 00:31:58.780
- THAT DOESN'T COUNT.


00:31:58.781 --> 00:32:00.349
IT DOESN'T COUNT
IF YOU HAVE TO BE THERE.


00:32:00.350 --> 00:32:01.983
- HEY, CHECK OUT THIS STAFF
I FOUND.


00:32:01.984 --> 00:32:03.852
- HOLY...


00:32:03.853 --> 00:32:05.654
- CHECK THAT BABY OUT.


00:32:05.655 --> 00:32:07.389
I THINK IT'S NATIVE AMERICAN.


00:32:07.390 --> 00:32:08.790
- NATIVE AMERICAN?


00:32:08.791 --> 00:32:11.093
WHAT DO YOU THINK THIS IS, LIKE,
A FALCON HEAD OR SOMETHING?


00:32:11.094 --> 00:32:14.663
- HEY, GET BACK HERE.


00:32:14.664 --> 00:32:18.734
[eerie music]


00:32:18.735 --> 00:32:21.403
- WHAT THE HELL?


00:32:21.404 --> 00:32:22.871
- THIS IS BADASS.


00:32:22.872 --> 00:32:25.040
- WHAT?


00:32:25.041 --> 00:32:27.175
- THIS WASN'T ALL
DUG UP BEFORE.


00:32:27.176 --> 00:32:28.744
- SO?


00:32:28.745 --> 00:32:30.178
- THIS IS WHERE I FOUND
THE STAFF.


00:32:30.179 --> 00:32:32.881
WHEN I PULLED IT OUT,
THERE WAS JUST A TINY HOLE.


00:32:32.882 --> 00:32:34.350
THERE WAS A RAUNCHY
FUCKING SMELL,


00:32:34.351 --> 00:32:37.018
BUT IT WASN'T ALL DUG UP
LIKE THIS.


00:32:37.019 --> 00:32:39.388
- WELL, SOMETIMES
WHEN I PULL IT OUT,


00:32:39.389 --> 00:32:40.723
THERE'S A RAUNCHY SMELL TOO.


00:32:40.724 --> 00:32:41.890
- YOU'RE FUCKING DISGUSTING.


00:32:41.891 --> 00:32:43.125
- I KNOW. I'M SORRY.


00:32:43.126 --> 00:32:45.093
- MAYBE, LIKE, A GOPHER DID THIS
OR SOMETHING.


00:32:45.094 --> 00:32:47.095
YOU KNOW, ANIMALS ARE ATTRACTED
TO STRONG SMELLS.


00:32:47.096 --> 00:32:48.530
- YEAH, REMEMBER
BACK IN HIGH SCHOOL


00:32:48.531 --> 00:32:50.232
WHEN I BURIED THAT WEED
IN MOM'S ROSE GARDEN


00:32:50.233 --> 00:32:51.233
AND MAGGIE DUG IT UP?


00:32:51.234 --> 00:32:52.234
- I DO REMEMBER THAT.


00:32:52.235 --> 00:32:53.669
YOU WANT TO KNOW WHY
I REMEMBER THAT?


00:32:53.670 --> 00:32:54.670
'CAUSE THAT WAS MY WEED.


00:32:54.671 --> 00:32:56.739
- NO, IT WASN'T.
WAS IT?


00:32:56.740 --> 00:32:58.073
FUCK, I LEARNED MY LESSON.


00:32:58.074 --> 00:33:00.208
NEVER HIDE THE KUSH
IN THE BUSH.


00:33:00.209 --> 00:33:01.510
GO FOR BIG.


00:33:01.511 --> 00:33:02.745
- HEY, LOOK.


00:33:02.746 --> 00:33:04.613
DON'T TELL THE GIRLS ABOUT THIS,
ALL RIGHT?


00:33:04.614 --> 00:33:06.181
I DON'T WANT TO GET THEM
ALL FREAKED OUT.


00:33:06.182 --> 00:33:07.416
- ALL RIGHT.
MY LIPS ARE SEALED.


00:33:07.417 --> 00:33:08.617
- OH, YEAH?
SO WERE ANNETTE'S.


00:33:08.618 --> 00:33:10.386
- COME ON, DUDE.
THAT WAS A LONG-ASS TIME AGO.


00:33:10.387 --> 00:33:11.787
SHE'S LIKE MY LITTLE SISTER NOW.


00:33:11.788 --> 00:33:13.589
- SO YEAH, YOU WANT TO FUCK
YOUR LITTLE SISTER?


00:33:13.590 --> 00:33:14.590
- YOU'RE DISGUSTING.


00:33:14.591 --> 00:33:15.891
- I SAID "LIKE"
MY LITTLE SISTER.


00:33:15.892 --> 00:33:16.892
JUST MEANS...
- SHUT UP.


00:33:16.893 --> 00:33:18.059
- IN THE ENGLISH LANGUAGE


00:33:18.060 --> 00:33:19.728
THAT SHE'S SIMILAR
BUT NOT EXACTLY--


00:33:19.729 --> 00:33:21.430
I'LL FUCK YOUR LITTLE SISTER,
THOUGH.


00:33:21.431 --> 00:33:22.665
- COME ON, MIKE.


00:33:22.666 --> 00:33:24.232
- SHE'S GOT BIG TITS
FOR A 14-YEAR-OLD.


00:33:24.233 --> 00:33:25.601
- WHAT?
- SHUT UP.


00:33:25.602 --> 00:33:26.702
SHE WAS IN A WHEELCHAIR.


00:33:31.240 --> 00:33:34.242
[eerie music]


00:33:34.243 --> 00:33:42.017
¶ ¶


00:33:43.085 --> 00:33:44.920
[car horn honks]


00:33:44.921 --> 00:33:47.756
- PAINT'S HERE.


00:33:51.961 --> 00:33:59.901
¶ ¶


00:34:06.643 --> 00:34:09.745
YOU GOT HERE FAST.


00:34:09.746 --> 00:34:12.481
- I DON'T...


00:34:12.482 --> 00:34:13.782
MIND GETTING OUT OF THE SHOP


00:34:13.783 --> 00:34:15.718
IF I'VE GOT AN EXCUSE FOR IT.


00:34:15.719 --> 00:34:17.252
- WELL, WE'RE HAPPY
TO BE YOUR EXCUSE.


00:34:17.253 --> 00:34:18.253
- YEAH.


00:34:18.254 --> 00:34:21.623
[laughter]


00:34:24.694 --> 00:34:27.195
- MR. PECK?


00:34:31.534 --> 00:34:33.169
[engine turns over]


00:34:33.170 --> 00:34:34.436
HEY.


00:34:34.437 --> 00:34:37.773
IS THERE SOMETHING I SHOULD KNOW
ABOUT THIS HOUSE?


00:34:37.774 --> 00:34:38.774
GOSH.


00:34:38.775 --> 00:34:40.176
- WHAT'S HIS PROBLEM?


00:34:40.177 --> 00:34:42.878
- SOMETHING FREAKED HIM OUT.


00:34:42.879 --> 00:34:45.447
SOMETHING REALLY SPOOKED HIM.


00:34:45.448 --> 00:34:47.850
- NAH, HE'S JUST PISSED
HE LET THIS PLACE


00:34:47.851 --> 00:34:49.585
SLIP THROUGH
HIS DIRTY OLD FINGERS.


00:34:49.586 --> 00:34:51.453
- I DON'T KNOW.


00:34:51.454 --> 00:34:52.888
HE LOOKED PRETTY SCARED.


00:34:52.889 --> 00:34:55.390
HERE, GIVE ME THAT.


00:34:55.391 --> 00:34:57.793
THANKS.


00:34:57.794 --> 00:35:00.629
THAT WAS SO WEIRD.


00:35:00.630 --> 00:35:01.997
WHAT ARE YOU CARRYING?


00:35:01.998 --> 00:35:04.233
NOTHING?
OF COURSE.


00:35:04.234 --> 00:35:05.534
- HEY, JEN.


00:35:05.535 --> 00:35:07.369
I BET I KNOW WHY HE WAS
ALL BITTER.


00:35:07.370 --> 00:35:09.404
HE PROBABLY WANTED HIS HANDS
ON ALL THE ANTIQUES.


00:35:09.405 --> 00:35:11.874
- ANTIQUES?
WHAT ANTIQUES?


00:35:11.875 --> 00:35:13.342
- IT'S A GOLD MINE, BROTHER.


00:35:13.343 --> 00:35:16.145
- STUPID FALCON HEAD.


00:35:16.146 --> 00:35:18.147
- HAVEN'T CHECKED THIS OUT
REALLY YET.


00:35:22.819 --> 00:35:25.221
- OH, MY GOD.


00:35:25.222 --> 00:35:26.756
[chuckles]


00:35:29.492 --> 00:35:30.893
OH, THIS HAS GOT TO BE
GOOD STUFF.


00:35:30.894 --> 00:35:34.563
- GIVE ME THAT.


00:35:34.564 --> 00:35:35.898
DUDE, YOU CAN'T DRINK
THIS STUFF.


00:35:35.899 --> 00:35:37.833
THIS IS, LIKE, $1,000 BOTTLE
OF WINE.


00:35:37.834 --> 00:35:39.301
- WHAT?
SHUT UP.


00:35:39.302 --> 00:35:42.571
- YOU, MY FRIEND,
HAVE HIT THE BOOZE JACKPOT.


00:35:42.572 --> 00:35:44.339
THESE REDNECKS GOT THEIR HANDS


00:35:44.340 --> 00:35:47.743
ON SOME PRETTY FUCKING RARE
FRENCH WINE.


00:35:47.744 --> 00:35:49.111
THIS IS--


00:35:49.112 --> 00:35:52.148
THIS DATES BACK TO...
FUCK,


00:35:52.149 --> 00:35:54.784
WHEN LINCOLN WAS IN OFFICE.


00:35:54.785 --> 00:35:56.318
- SHIT.


00:35:59.122 --> 00:36:01.257
- OH, LOOK.
WE CAN DESIGN OUR OWN CLOTHES.


00:36:01.258 --> 00:36:04.526
- OH, LOOK.
WE CAN HAVE TEA PARTIES TOO.


00:36:04.527 --> 00:36:06.996
- MOST GIRLS LIKE TO DESIGN
THEIR OWN CLOTHES.


00:36:06.997 --> 00:36:10.099
- WELL, I LIKE 10-YEAR-OLDS
IN CHINA TO SEW MINE.


00:36:10.100 --> 00:36:11.366
[laughter]


00:36:11.367 --> 00:36:12.467
- AND YOU'RE GOING TO HELL.


00:36:12.468 --> 00:36:13.669
- YOU KNOW WHAT THEY SAY:


00:36:13.670 --> 00:36:15.737
HEAVEN FOR THE WEATHER,
HELL FOR THE COMPANY.


00:36:15.738 --> 00:36:17.773
- [laughing]


00:36:17.774 --> 00:36:19.508
SPEAKING OF HEAVEN AND HELL,


00:36:19.509 --> 00:36:22.711
HOW'S IT GOING WITH YOU AND KEN?


00:36:22.712 --> 00:36:24.113
- WELL...
- WELL?


00:36:24.114 --> 00:36:26.248
- I JUST WEAR
THAT SLAVE LEIA COSTUME,


00:36:26.249 --> 00:36:28.350
AND I GET ALL THE ATTENTION
I WANT.


00:36:28.351 --> 00:36:29.351
- OH.


00:36:29.352 --> 00:36:31.386
- I HAD A THOUGHT.
- MM-HMM.


00:36:31.387 --> 00:36:33.823
- YOU KNOW WHAT WOULD BE FUN?
- NO.


00:36:33.824 --> 00:36:35.791
- A LITTLE MIKE AND ANNETTE
ACTION.


00:36:35.792 --> 00:36:37.592
- OOH, YEAH.
- NO!


00:36:37.593 --> 00:36:39.028
- YEAH!
- YOU USED TO THINK HE WAS HOT.


00:36:39.029 --> 00:36:40.029
- YEAH, WHEN WAS FIVE.


00:36:40.030 --> 00:36:41.096
- AND YOU'RE NEWLY SINGLE.


00:36:41.097 --> 00:36:43.065
AND--NO.
IT'LL BE FUN.


00:36:43.066 --> 00:36:45.835
- HE HAS MORE HAIR ON HIS BACK
THAN HE HAS ON HIS HEAD.


00:36:45.836 --> 00:36:47.036
- I KNOW, BUT THEN


00:36:47.037 --> 00:36:48.737
YOU COULD JUST RUN
YOUR FINGERS THROUGH IT.


00:36:48.738 --> 00:36:52.141
- A LITTLE TESTOSTERONE OVERDOSE
WOULD BE GOOD FOR YOU.


00:36:52.142 --> 00:36:54.176
- IT'S GOING TO BE
A LONG WEEKEND.


00:36:54.177 --> 00:36:57.046
- I WOULD NOT BANG MIKE
TO SAVE HIS LIFE.


00:36:57.047 --> 00:36:58.747
- 10 BUCKS SHE DOES.


00:36:58.748 --> 00:37:00.349
- I'LL TAKE THAT ACTION.


00:37:00.350 --> 00:37:03.418
- YOU ARE SO IMMATURE.


00:37:03.419 --> 00:37:05.054
- BANG HIM,


00:37:05.055 --> 00:37:06.455
AND I'LL SPLIT IT WITH YOU.


00:37:06.456 --> 00:37:07.957
- OH!


00:37:07.958 --> 00:37:09.624
EW!


00:37:09.625 --> 00:37:10.826
- [sniffing]


00:37:10.827 --> 00:37:11.961
OH.


00:37:11.962 --> 00:37:13.562
- IT SMELLS LIKE SATAN'S BALLS
IN HERE.


00:37:13.563 --> 00:37:14.629
[coughs]


00:37:14.630 --> 00:37:16.398
I'M GONNA GO CHECK
ON THE GIRLS.


00:37:16.399 --> 00:37:17.799
- PUSSY.


00:37:17.800 --> 00:37:20.702
- YEAH, I THINK I'VE HAD ENOUGH
FOR ONE DAY TOO.


00:37:20.703 --> 00:37:21.770
- COME ON, MAN.
NO. COME ON.


00:37:21.771 --> 00:37:22.771
WE GOT TO GO BACK THERE.


00:37:22.772 --> 00:37:23.805
THERE'S PROBABLY, LIKE,


00:37:23.806 --> 00:37:25.274
A DIAMOND MINE IN THERE
OR SOMETHING.


00:37:25.275 --> 00:37:26.942
- I DON'T EVEN THINK I HAVE
THE KEY FOR THIS.


00:37:26.943 --> 00:37:28.077
YEAH, NO, I DON'T.


00:37:28.078 --> 00:37:30.079
- WHAT?


00:37:30.080 --> 00:37:31.313
FINE.


00:37:31.314 --> 00:37:34.316
[tense music]


00:37:34.317 --> 00:37:39.321
¶ ¶


00:37:39.322 --> 00:37:41.156
- [laughing]


00:37:41.157 --> 00:37:42.524
OH, MY GOD!


00:37:42.525 --> 00:37:44.426
THAT WAS FUCKING PERFECT.


00:37:44.427 --> 00:37:46.262
DUDE, YOU TWO WERE SO SCARED.


00:37:46.263 --> 00:37:48.163
YOU ALMOST SHIT
EACH OTHER'S PANTS.


00:37:48.164 --> 00:37:49.564
- FUCK YOU.


00:37:49.565 --> 00:37:51.200
- WHERE THE HELL
DID YOU GET THIS?


00:37:51.201 --> 00:37:52.501
- I SAW IT WHEN I FIRST CAME IN.


00:37:52.502 --> 00:37:54.469
I'VE BEEN WAITING
TO SCARE YOU GUYS WITH IT.


00:37:54.470 --> 00:37:56.505
- [laughs mockingly]


00:37:56.506 --> 00:37:57.639
- OH, SHUT UP.


00:37:57.640 --> 00:37:59.108
THE ADRENALINE'S A RUSH.
YOU KNOW IT.


00:37:59.109 --> 00:38:00.342
- YEAH, WELL, PAYBACK'S A BITCH.


00:38:00.343 --> 00:38:02.044
- KICK HIS ASS, DUDE.


00:38:04.414 --> 00:38:06.882
- SPREAD 'EM.


00:38:06.883 --> 00:38:10.452
HELP! HELP!
RAPE! RAPE!


00:38:12.522 --> 00:38:17.459
- JUST WHAT THE DOCTOR ORDERED.


00:38:17.460 --> 00:38:19.528
- OKAY, LADIES.


00:38:19.529 --> 00:38:22.831
WHAT DO YOU THINK,
CHIC OR SHRIEK?


00:38:22.832 --> 00:38:25.401
both: SHRIEK.


00:38:25.402 --> 00:38:28.103
- OH, WOW.


00:38:28.104 --> 00:38:32.774
- HEY, THIS WOMAN IS WEARING
THAT DRESS.


00:38:34.844 --> 00:38:37.879
CHECK THIS OUT.


00:38:37.880 --> 00:38:41.083
- OH, WOW.
THAT'S SLIGHTLY CREEPY.


00:38:41.084 --> 00:38:42.851
- NO, IT'S TOTALLY CREEPY.


00:38:42.852 --> 00:38:43.953
- OH, MY GOD, YOU GUYS.


00:38:43.954 --> 00:38:45.587
YOU HAVE TO COME
CHECK OUT THIS TUB.


00:38:45.588 --> 00:38:50.225
IT'S AWESOME.


00:38:50.226 --> 00:38:52.094
- LOOK AT YOU GETTING COMFY.


00:38:52.095 --> 00:38:53.495
- I CALL DIBS.


00:38:53.496 --> 00:38:55.998
- OH, WELL, I BELIEVE
MY OWNING THE HOUSE


00:38:55.999 --> 00:38:57.266
TRUMPS YOUR DIBS.


00:38:57.267 --> 00:38:58.400
- OVER MY DEAD BODY.


00:38:58.401 --> 00:38:59.401
- [laughs]


00:38:59.402 --> 00:39:01.536
- GUYS, COME LOOK AT THIS.


00:39:04.607 --> 00:39:07.376
THERE IS SO MUCH OF THIS.


00:39:07.377 --> 00:39:09.411
- IS THAT STUFF REAL?


00:39:09.412 --> 00:39:10.779
- WHO CARES?


00:39:10.780 --> 00:39:14.183
THE COSTUME SET'S WORTH
A FORTUNE TOO THESE DAYS.


00:39:14.184 --> 00:39:15.284
- HEY, JEN, WHAT DO YOU THINK?


00:39:15.285 --> 00:39:18.220
IS THIS TOO MUCH FOR ME?


00:39:18.221 --> 00:39:20.755
JEN?


00:39:20.756 --> 00:39:21.890
WHAT IS THAT?


00:39:21.891 --> 00:39:26.395
- LOOKS LIKE
MRS. TUCKER'S DIARY.


00:39:26.396 --> 00:39:29.531
LYDIA BEAUMONT,


00:39:29.532 --> 00:39:31.066
WHOEVER THAT IS.


00:39:31.067 --> 00:39:34.103
- FAMILY MEMBER MAYBE?
- YEAH.


00:39:34.104 --> 00:39:35.304
- WHAT DOES IT SAY?


00:39:35.305 --> 00:39:37.672
- CHECK THIS OUT.


00:39:37.673 --> 00:39:40.709
"LEONARD'S CONDITION WORSENS
WITH EACH DAY.


00:39:40.710 --> 00:39:42.978
"SINCE THE DAY MRS. TUCKER
CUT LEONARD'S SCALP,


00:39:42.979 --> 00:39:44.813
"THE INFECTION HAS SPREAD FASTER


00:39:44.814 --> 00:39:46.681
"THAN ANY MEDICINE OR PRAYER
CAN HOLD IT.


00:39:46.682 --> 00:39:48.850
"ANOTHER BAD DAY FOR LEONARD.


00:39:48.851 --> 00:39:51.920
"I CANNOT BELIEVE HIS CONDITION
HAS GOTTEN SO GRAVE.


00:39:51.921 --> 00:39:54.556
"HE IS NO LONGER ALLOWED
TO ATTEND SCHOOL...


00:39:54.557 --> 00:39:56.558
- IF LEONARD CANNOT GO ON,


00:39:56.559 --> 00:39:58.627
NEITHER COULD I.


00:39:58.628 --> 00:40:02.197
- "I COULDN'T BARE TO OUTLIVE
MY OWN CHILD."


00:40:02.198 --> 00:40:05.501
- OH, IT DOES NOT SAY THAT.


00:40:05.502 --> 00:40:07.869
- WOULD YOU STOP?
I GET NIGHTMARES.


00:40:07.870 --> 00:40:11.606
- [laughs]


00:40:11.607 --> 00:40:12.641
FINE.


00:40:12.642 --> 00:40:13.675
LET'S GO FIND THE BOYS.


00:40:13.676 --> 00:40:15.077
WE HAVE SO MUCH CLEANING
TO DO.


00:40:15.078 --> 00:40:17.012
- YEAH, THEY'RE GONNA WANT
TO CLEAN.


00:40:17.013 --> 00:40:19.848
I DO NOT THINK ANYBODY'S
GONNA BE DOING ANY CLEANING.


00:40:19.849 --> 00:40:21.183
- YEAH, WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?


00:40:21.184 --> 00:40:25.187
IF THEY WANT ANY MORE BEER,
THEY'LL CLEAN.


00:40:25.188 --> 00:40:28.190
[eerie music]


00:40:28.191 --> 00:40:29.791
¶ ¶


00:40:29.792 --> 00:40:32.794
[lively percussive music]


00:40:32.795 --> 00:40:40.735
¶ ¶


00:40:45.875 --> 00:40:47.376
klink!


00:40:47.377 --> 00:40:48.377
- [moaning]


00:40:48.378 --> 00:40:50.179
- [shushing]
- OH, BABY.


00:40:53.783 --> 00:40:54.983
- [shushing]


00:40:54.984 --> 00:40:56.118
YOU ARE SO FUCKING LOUD.


00:40:56.119 --> 00:40:58.287
- OH, WAS I?
I'M SORRY.


00:41:02.024 --> 00:41:05.894
¶ ¶


00:41:05.895 --> 00:41:10.632
- [breathing heavily]


00:41:10.633 --> 00:41:13.202
- YOU ARE AN ANGEL, LYDIA.


00:41:13.203 --> 00:41:15.471
- YOU DO NOT TREAT ME
LIKE ONE.


00:41:15.472 --> 00:41:16.972
- I DO.


00:41:16.973 --> 00:41:19.108
- ONLY WHEN WE ARE ALONE.


00:41:19.109 --> 00:41:20.242
- IF THEY FIND OUT ABOUT US,


00:41:20.243 --> 00:41:22.677
THEY MIGHT WANT TO TAKE LEONARD.


00:41:22.678 --> 00:41:26.047
- I KNOW.


00:41:26.048 --> 00:41:28.417
- I'M TAKING CARE OF HIM,
AREN'T I?


00:41:28.418 --> 00:41:30.452
- MON FILS,


00:41:30.453 --> 00:41:32.754
HE IS NOT DOING MUCH GOOD.


00:41:32.755 --> 00:41:36.691
- ABRAHAM!


00:41:36.692 --> 00:41:39.561
ABRAHAM!


00:41:39.562 --> 00:41:40.896
ABRAHAM!


00:41:45.735 --> 00:41:46.935
WHERE IS SHE?


00:41:46.936 --> 00:41:48.170
- GET BACK IN THE HOUSE,
CLAIRE.


00:41:48.171 --> 00:41:50.505
- DON'T YOU EVEN DARE.


00:41:50.506 --> 00:41:54.009
ISN'T YOUR RETARD SON
PROOF ENOUGH THAT IT'S WRONG?


00:42:00.884 --> 00:42:03.886
[dramatic music]


00:42:03.887 --> 00:42:10.259
¶ ¶


00:42:10.260 --> 00:42:14.897
LYDIA, THERE ARE CONSEQUENCES
YOU HAVE TO ACCEPT.


00:42:14.898 --> 00:42:17.966
I TOLERATED YOU
AND YOUR BASTARD CHILD.


00:42:17.967 --> 00:42:20.068
YOU SHOULD HAVE LEFT
WELL ENOUGH ALONE.


00:42:20.069 --> 00:42:22.570
¶ ¶


00:42:22.571 --> 00:42:24.773
[choking]


00:42:29.179 --> 00:42:30.445
crack!


00:42:58.541 --> 00:43:01.276
[gentle acoustic guitar]


00:43:01.277 --> 00:43:03.278
- WOW, IT IS GORGEOUS OUT HERE,
ISN'T IT?


00:43:03.279 --> 00:43:05.347
- YES, IT IS.


00:43:05.348 --> 00:43:08.683
- JUST WAIT TILL WE'RE DONE
WITH RENOVATIONS.


00:43:10.453 --> 00:43:12.154
- NOTHING LIKE WASHING DOWN
A CHEESEBURGER


00:43:12.155 --> 00:43:13.788
WITH A $1,000 BOTTLE OF WINE.


00:43:13.789 --> 00:43:16.191
- HEY, GIVE ME
THAT LEFT BOTTLE.


00:43:16.192 --> 00:43:17.359
IT'S THE LAST ONE.


00:43:17.360 --> 00:43:18.827
THE REST ARE GOING
TO THE AUCTION.


00:43:18.828 --> 00:43:20.495
- DOES ANYBODY WANT
ANOTHER BEER?


00:43:20.496 --> 00:43:23.031
- I DO.
- NO, THANKS.


00:43:28.537 --> 00:43:30.172
- THAT'S GOOD STUFF.


00:43:30.173 --> 00:43:35.210
¶ ¶


00:43:35.211 --> 00:43:38.213
- [vocalizing]


00:43:38.214 --> 00:43:45.520
¶ ¶


00:43:54.931 --> 00:43:56.932
- SOMETHING WRONG?


00:43:56.933 --> 00:43:59.734
- HM.


00:43:59.735 --> 00:44:03.238
JUST THINKING ABOUT THE TUCKERS.


00:44:03.239 --> 00:44:07.776
THEY HAD EVERYTHING
YOU COULD WANT, YOU KNOW.


00:44:07.777 --> 00:44:12.114
AND FOR WHAT?


00:44:12.115 --> 00:44:14.383
I BET THEY WERE NICE PEOPLE.


00:44:14.384 --> 00:44:15.550
- [burps]


00:44:15.551 --> 00:44:17.019
WELL, IT DOESN'T MATTER NOW,
DOES IT?


00:44:17.020 --> 00:44:18.987
THEY'RE DEAD.


00:44:23.426 --> 00:44:26.295
- I WONDER IF THEY WERE HAPPY.


00:44:26.296 --> 00:44:28.063
- I HOPE THEY WERE HAPPY.


00:44:28.064 --> 00:44:29.497
- ME TOO.


00:44:29.498 --> 00:44:31.400
- I MEAN, LOOK AT THIS PLACE:


00:44:31.401 --> 00:44:32.935
ALL THIS LAND


00:44:32.936 --> 00:44:34.736
AND ALL THE WINE.


00:44:34.737 --> 00:44:35.870
COME ON.


00:44:35.871 --> 00:44:38.706
HOW COULD ANYTHING GO WRONG?


00:44:38.707 --> 00:44:41.476
- WELL, WHATEVER HAPPENED
TO THEM,


00:44:41.477 --> 00:44:43.711
I GUESS IT'S NOT
OUR FAULT, HUH?


00:44:43.712 --> 00:44:46.148
- YOU'RE JUST BRINGING
SOME LIGHT BACK INTO THIS PLACE.


00:44:46.149 --> 00:44:47.316
THAT'S ALL IT NEEDS.


00:44:47.317 --> 00:44:48.951
- WOW, BABE.
THAT'S DEEP.


00:44:48.952 --> 00:44:52.520
- OCCASIONALLY I DO LEAVE
THE DEEP END.


00:44:52.521 --> 00:44:53.788
SHALLOW END.


00:44:53.789 --> 00:44:54.789
[laughter]


00:44:54.790 --> 00:44:57.459
GOT THAT SAYING WRONG.


00:44:57.460 --> 00:44:59.794
- SENATOR KEN SAYS
IT CAN HAPPEN.


00:44:59.795 --> 00:45:02.998
- YOU KNOW, MIKE WAS SAYING
THAT THE BARN WAS PRETTY COOL.


00:45:02.999 --> 00:45:06.101
YOU WANT TO CHECK IT OUT?


00:45:06.102 --> 00:45:07.469
- WHAT?


00:45:07.470 --> 00:45:12.607
- BY CHECK IT OUT,
I MEAN HAVE SEX.


00:45:12.608 --> 00:45:14.042
[laughter]


00:45:14.043 --> 00:45:17.179
- [inRussian accent] IN THIS
CASE, WE WILL CHECK IT OUT.


00:45:17.180 --> 00:45:20.182
- MMM, YOU BIG
RUSSIAN MINX, YOU.


00:45:20.183 --> 00:45:22.784
[laughter]


00:45:22.785 --> 00:45:25.087
- WATCH OUT FOR
THE AUTOMATIC MILKING MACHINE.


00:45:25.088 --> 00:45:26.921
IT STICKS A LITTLE.


00:45:26.922 --> 00:45:28.190
- OH.


00:45:28.191 --> 00:45:30.125
YOU KNOW WHAT?
YOU'VE HAD ENOUGH.


00:45:30.126 --> 00:45:32.327
WOW, BABE.


00:45:32.328 --> 00:45:35.464
THAT IS AMAZING.
LET'S GO TO BED.


00:45:35.465 --> 00:45:38.367
YOU ARE SO DONE.


00:45:38.368 --> 00:45:42.004
- OKAY.


00:45:42.005 --> 00:45:43.238
- WE'LL SEE YOU TOMORROW.


00:45:43.239 --> 00:45:44.439
- GOOD NIGHT.


00:45:44.440 --> 00:45:46.441
- GOOD NIGHT.


00:45:46.442 --> 00:45:48.276
- HEY, MAN, WHAT DO YOU WANT ME
TO DO WITH THE FIRE?


00:45:48.277 --> 00:45:50.845
- UM, JUST THROW A LITTLE BEER
ON IT.


00:45:50.846 --> 00:45:52.847
- [laughs]


00:45:52.848 --> 00:45:54.883
- NIGHT.
- NIGHT.


00:45:56.952 --> 00:46:01.189
¶ ¶


00:46:01.190 --> 00:46:02.824
- HUH!


00:46:09.899 --> 00:46:11.699
- I'M KIND OF TIRED.


00:46:11.700 --> 00:46:14.736
- ME TOO.


00:46:14.737 --> 00:46:17.205
- A MASSAGE WOULD BE NICE.


00:46:17.206 --> 00:46:18.373
- OH, YEAH?


00:46:18.374 --> 00:46:20.409
GOT SOME SORE MUSCLES.
NEED WORKIN'?


00:46:20.410 --> 00:46:22.477
- [laughs]


00:46:22.478 --> 00:46:23.645
- I COULD TEACH YOU A FEW THINGS


00:46:23.646 --> 00:46:25.047
I LEARNED IN THAILAND
LAST SUMMER.


00:46:25.048 --> 00:46:27.382
- OH, GOD.


00:46:27.383 --> 00:46:30.385
- BUT FIRST,
YOU HAVE TO GET NAKED.


00:46:30.386 --> 00:46:32.120
WELL, BOTH OF US.


00:46:32.121 --> 00:46:38.260
AND THEN YOU WALK BAREFOOT
ALL OVER MY BACK,


00:46:38.261 --> 00:46:41.063
AND THEN YOU


00:46:41.064 --> 00:46:43.665
STEAL ALL THE MONEY
FROM MY WALLET.


00:46:43.666 --> 00:46:46.034
- [laughs]


00:46:54.544 --> 00:46:57.212
COME ON.


00:46:57.213 --> 00:46:59.114
- WHAT ABOUT THE FIRE?


00:46:59.115 --> 00:47:01.783
- OH, I THINK IT'LL BURN
ITSELF OUT.


00:47:01.784 --> 00:47:04.186
- I THINK YOU'RE RIGHT.


00:47:04.187 --> 00:47:05.620
- COME HERE.


00:47:05.621 --> 00:47:07.789
- [in Russian accent] DO YOU
WANT TO SHOW ME YOUR NEW GUN,


00:47:07.790 --> 00:47:10.758
MR. BIG RUSSIAN
ILLEGAL ARMS MAN?


00:47:10.759 --> 00:47:12.394
- [in Russian accent]
YES, AND I THINK


00:47:12.395 --> 00:47:14.329
YOU'RE GOING TO LOVE
THE NEW ATTACHMENTS.


00:47:14.330 --> 00:47:15.897
- OOH, LET'S GO UPSTAIRS.


00:47:15.898 --> 00:47:18.766
- STAY IN CHARACTER.


00:47:18.767 --> 00:47:21.769
[ominous music]


00:47:21.770 --> 00:47:29.711
¶ ¶


00:47:58.874 --> 00:48:03.245
[bird squawking]


00:48:03.246 --> 00:48:11.186
¶ ¶


00:48:16.959 --> 00:48:20.094
[rustling]


00:48:20.095 --> 00:48:28.036
¶ ¶


00:48:32.708 --> 00:48:37.979
[both moaning]


00:48:37.980 --> 00:48:41.483
- THAT WAS TOO QUICK.


00:48:41.484 --> 00:48:43.951
- HEY, WELL, YOU KNOW,


00:48:43.952 --> 00:48:46.588
I WAS BORN WITH
THE SPORTS MODEL;


00:48:46.589 --> 00:48:50.292
I MIGHT NOT BE AS BIG,
BUT I'M TWICE AS FAST.


00:48:50.293 --> 00:48:54.095
- JUST WHAT EVERY WOMAN WANTS.


00:48:54.096 --> 00:48:55.430
- I GOTTA GO.
I GOTTA RECOUP.


00:48:55.431 --> 00:48:58.300
YOU KNOW, I GOTTA GO--
I GOTTA GO MAKE TINKLE TINKLE.


00:48:58.301 --> 00:49:00.034
- HURRY UP.


00:49:00.035 --> 00:49:03.938
DADDY'S GIRL'S READY
FOR THE NEXT DEMONSTRATION.


00:49:03.939 --> 00:49:06.841
[laughs]


00:49:09.912 --> 00:49:12.447
- [grumbling]


00:49:21.524 --> 00:49:23.558
[urinating]


00:49:32.635 --> 00:49:36.871
OH, YOU JUST COULDN'T WAIT
FOR A SECOND HELPING, HUH?


00:49:43.512 --> 00:49:45.012
crack!


00:49:53.756 --> 00:49:56.691
- MR. ARMS DEALER?


00:50:00.395 --> 00:50:02.630
WHAT'S TAKING YOU SO LONG?


00:50:02.631 --> 00:50:05.633
[ominous music]


00:50:05.634 --> 00:50:13.575
¶ ¶


00:50:27.490 --> 00:50:31.292
HELLO?


00:50:31.293 --> 00:50:34.128
KEN!


00:50:34.129 --> 00:50:37.465
- [grunting]


00:50:37.466 --> 00:50:40.101
- THERE YOU ARE.


00:50:40.102 --> 00:50:42.236
COME ON.


00:50:42.237 --> 00:50:45.874
MY DADDY MIGHT GET HOME
ANY MINUTE NOW.


00:50:57.185 --> 00:51:04.759
DADDY'S LITTLE GIRL
IS GETTING VERY, VERY FEISTY.


00:51:16.271 --> 00:51:18.139
[tense music]


00:51:18.140 --> 00:51:22.410
[screaming]


00:51:25.480 --> 00:51:28.449
[fire crackling]


00:51:38.561 --> 00:51:41.095
- [exhales deeply]


00:51:47.169 --> 00:51:49.837
WHAT THE HELL?


00:52:06.922 --> 00:52:09.958
"LEONARD'S DISEASE SHOWS
NO HOPE FOR REMISSION.


00:52:09.959 --> 00:52:15.063
"TODAY HIS FATHER EXPELLED HIM
FROM THE MAIN LIVING QUARTERS.


00:52:15.064 --> 00:52:20.735
"HE IS TO LIVE IN THE BASEMENT,
EFFECTIVE IMMEDIATELY.


00:52:20.736 --> 00:52:22.971
"IF HIS CONDITION
CONTINUES TO DIGRESS,


00:52:22.972 --> 00:52:26.874
"TUCKER SWORE HE WOULD TAKE
MATTERS INTO HIS OWN HANDS.


00:52:26.875 --> 00:52:30.478
"HE THINKS ITS CRUEL TO LET HIM
LIVE ON THIS WAY,


00:52:30.479 --> 00:52:32.680
BUT WHAT CHOICE DO WE HAVE?"


00:52:39.888 --> 00:52:47.561
[speaking French]


00:52:47.562 --> 00:52:50.131
WHAT IS THIS?


00:52:50.132 --> 00:52:54.468
WHY IS THE REST OF THIS
IN FRENCH?


00:52:54.469 --> 00:52:55.937
IS THIS VOODOO?


00:52:55.938 --> 00:52:58.139
[clamoring]


00:53:00.208 --> 00:53:03.210
[eerie music]


00:53:03.211 --> 00:53:11.152
¶ ¶


00:53:46.689 --> 00:53:49.590
[birds chirping]


00:53:54.262 --> 00:53:55.930
KEN?


00:53:55.931 --> 00:53:57.565
HILLARY?


00:54:04.639 --> 00:54:07.641
[eerie music]


00:54:07.642 --> 00:54:15.583
¶ ¶


00:54:26.494 --> 00:54:31.265
[sizzling]


00:54:31.266 --> 00:54:32.633
- YUP.


00:54:41.710 --> 00:54:43.010
- HAVE YOU GUYS SEEN
KEN AND HILL?


00:54:43.011 --> 00:54:45.079
- I THINK THEY MUST HAVE GONE
INTO TOWN FOR BREAKFAST.


00:54:45.080 --> 00:54:48.515
- SUCKS FOR THEM.


00:54:48.516 --> 00:54:52.319
- HEY, THANK YOU FOR CLEANING UP
AFTER ALL OF US LAST NIGHT.


00:54:52.320 --> 00:54:53.387
- WHAT DID I DO?


00:54:53.388 --> 00:54:54.388
- NO?
- NO.


00:54:54.389 --> 00:54:55.757
- BABE?


00:54:55.758 --> 00:54:59.026
- UH, YEAH, YEAH.


00:54:59.027 --> 00:55:00.228
NO.


00:55:00.229 --> 00:55:01.229
- [laughing]


00:55:01.230 --> 00:55:02.730
I DIDN'T THINK SO.


00:55:02.731 --> 00:55:05.399
BUT YOU MEAN TO TELL ME THAT
KEN AND HILLARY CLEANED UP?


00:55:05.400 --> 00:55:07.301
- I DON'T THINK THAT SOUNDS
LIKE HILLARY.


00:55:07.302 --> 00:55:10.238
- NO.


00:55:10.239 --> 00:55:12.640
- A LITTLE SALT AND PEPPER
FOR YOU.


00:55:12.641 --> 00:55:17.344
- OH, EVAN, I DON'T USUALLY
EAT BREAKFAST THIS EARLY.


00:55:19.948 --> 00:55:20.948
- JEN?


00:55:20.949 --> 00:55:23.050
- OH, THANK YOU.


00:55:23.051 --> 00:55:25.253
OKAY.


00:55:27.322 --> 00:55:29.857
SO WHAT ARE YOU BOYS UP TO
TODAY?


00:55:29.858 --> 00:55:31.859
- WELL, WHEN MIKE
FINALLY WAKES UP,


00:55:31.860 --> 00:55:33.194
WE'RE GONNA WORK
ON THE WIRING.


00:55:33.195 --> 00:55:34.361
- ALL RIGHT.


00:55:34.362 --> 00:55:35.997
WELL, UM, I'M GOING TO GO
INTO TOWN


00:55:35.998 --> 00:55:36.998
AND RUN A FEW ERRANDS.


00:55:36.999 --> 00:55:39.433
- OH, CAN I COME?
- YEAH.


00:55:39.434 --> 00:55:40.534
YOU WANT ANYTHING?


00:55:40.535 --> 00:55:42.303
- YEAH, CAN I GET
A DOUBLE TALL LATTE


00:55:42.304 --> 00:55:43.971
AND A LOW-FAT APRICOT MUFFIN?


00:55:43.972 --> 00:55:45.439
- RIGHT.


00:55:45.440 --> 00:55:48.442
HOW ABOUT A BIG OLD PLATE
OF SOME CHITLINS AND CRAWFISH?


00:55:48.443 --> 00:55:50.644
- MMM.
CRAWFISH.


00:55:50.645 --> 00:55:51.979
- [laughs]


00:55:51.980 --> 00:55:54.182
THANK YOU SO MUCH FOR BREAKFAST.
THAT WAS REALLY SWEET.


00:55:54.183 --> 00:55:57.118
- MM-HMM.


00:55:57.119 --> 00:56:00.621
- BYE.
- HA!


00:56:00.622 --> 00:56:01.622
- BYE.


00:56:01.623 --> 00:56:04.625
[pleasant mandolin music]


00:56:04.626 --> 00:56:12.566
¶ ¶


00:56:16.471 --> 00:56:19.206
- GOD BLESS AMERICA.


00:56:19.207 --> 00:56:20.541
LET'S EAT.


00:56:20.542 --> 00:56:22.877
- YEAH, HEY, PICK UP
WHATEVER YOU THINK WE NEED.


00:56:22.878 --> 00:56:24.612
I'M JUST GONNA GO
CHECK OUT SOMETHING.


00:56:24.613 --> 00:56:26.614
- COOL.


00:56:26.615 --> 00:56:34.555
¶ ¶


00:56:42.597 --> 00:56:45.599
[eerie music]


00:56:45.600 --> 00:56:50.705
¶ ¶


00:56:50.706 --> 00:56:52.807
MR. PECK?


00:57:09.892 --> 00:57:11.959
MR. PECK?


00:57:22.037 --> 00:57:24.038
MR. PECK?


00:57:38.887 --> 00:57:42.757
- FIND WHAT YOU'RE LOOKING FOR?


00:57:42.758 --> 00:57:44.826
- I'M SORRY.


00:57:44.827 --> 00:57:48.162
I GUESS I'M NOT USED TO SEEING
WHERE MY FOOD COMES FROM.


00:57:51.834 --> 00:57:54.235
- THAT'S WHY WE, UH--


00:57:54.236 --> 00:57:56.738
THAT'S WHY WE DO IT OUT HERE.


00:57:56.739 --> 00:57:59.107
WANT A DRINK?


00:57:59.108 --> 00:58:02.543
- I'M GOOD.


00:58:02.544 --> 00:58:04.378
- I KNOW WHY YOU'RE HERE.


00:58:04.379 --> 00:58:06.781
- I WANT TO KNOW
WHY YOU RAN YESTERDAY.


00:58:06.782 --> 00:58:08.616
- I HAD TO GET TO WORK.


00:58:08.617 --> 00:58:10.351
- MR. PECK, I KNOW
THAT THERE'S SOMETHING


00:58:10.352 --> 00:58:13.320
THAT YOU'RE NOT TELLING ME.


00:58:13.321 --> 00:58:15.056
I FOUND A DIARY.


00:58:15.057 --> 00:58:17.191
IT'S A WOMAN'S:


00:58:17.192 --> 00:58:18.159
LYDIA BEAUMONT.


00:58:23.966 --> 00:58:26.500
YOU KNEW HER.


00:58:29.772 --> 00:58:32.073
- I KILLED HER.


00:58:34.943 --> 00:58:36.878
- WHY?


00:58:36.879 --> 00:58:38.813
- GIVE ME MY BABY!


00:58:38.814 --> 00:58:40.882
[gunshot]


00:58:40.883 --> 00:58:42.884
- SHE WAS A WITCH.


00:58:42.885 --> 00:58:43.985
- THERE'S NO SUCH THING.


00:58:43.986 --> 00:58:45.286
- I WOULD HAVE SAID
THE SAME THING


00:58:45.287 --> 00:58:47.621
IF I HAVEN'T SEEN IT
WITH MY OWN EYES.


00:58:47.622 --> 00:58:49.423
HELL, I EVEN DEFENDED HER.


00:58:49.424 --> 00:58:54.162
WHEN THE ANIMALS,
WHEN THEY CAME UP MISSING,


00:58:54.163 --> 00:58:57.131
PEOPLE SAID IT WAS
FOR HER VOODOO.


00:58:57.132 --> 00:58:58.465
I SAID IT WAS A FOX.


00:58:58.466 --> 00:59:00.434
WELL, I WAS WRONG.


00:59:00.435 --> 00:59:02.436
- SHE WAS KILLING
FARM ANIMALS?


00:59:02.437 --> 00:59:06.407
- SACRIFICING THEM,
MORE LIKE IT.


00:59:06.408 --> 00:59:07.875
I MEAN, MAYBE
IT WOULD HAVE BEEN OKAY


00:59:07.876 --> 00:59:11.078
IF IT STAYED
WITH CHICKENS AND GOATS,


00:59:11.079 --> 00:59:14.248
BUT THEN THAT'S WHEN
THE TOWNFOLK


00:59:14.249 --> 00:59:16.350
TOOK THE LAW
INTO THEIR OWN HANDS.


00:59:16.351 --> 00:59:18.352
THE BOY GOT SICK,


00:59:18.353 --> 00:59:20.822
UGLY SICK.


00:59:20.823 --> 00:59:24.658
PEOPLE SAID THAT
IT MADE HER MAD,


00:59:24.659 --> 00:59:26.460
CRAZY.


00:59:26.461 --> 00:59:30.198
- LEONARD, RIGHT?
- YEAH. LEONARD.


00:59:32.968 --> 00:59:38.072
- WHAT WAS WRONG WITH HIM?


00:59:38.073 --> 00:59:40.107
- HE WAS DEVIL-TOUCHED.


00:59:40.108 --> 00:59:41.843
IT'S THE ONLY WORD
TO DESCRIBE HIM--


00:59:41.844 --> 00:59:43.744
HIM AND HIS MOTHER.


00:59:48.150 --> 00:59:49.250
- [crying]


00:59:49.251 --> 00:59:51.785
- SHE STOLE MY BABY.


00:59:51.786 --> 00:59:53.654
SACRIFICED HIM
IN THE NAME OF MAGIC,


00:59:53.655 --> 00:59:59.626
ALL TO SAVE THAT EVIL
BASTARD OF HERS.


00:59:59.627 --> 01:00:01.863
THE ONLY THING IN THE WORLD
THAT I WANTED


01:00:01.864 --> 01:00:04.765
WAS TO SAVE MY BABY,


01:00:04.766 --> 01:00:09.536
AND THAT ONE WAS TOO LATE
FOR THAT.


01:00:09.537 --> 01:00:14.041
ALL I WANTED TO SEE
WAS HER BURNED.


01:00:14.042 --> 01:00:17.912
- [screaming]


01:00:27.155 --> 01:00:30.992
- YOU GOTTA LEAVE THAT HOUSE.


01:00:30.993 --> 01:00:35.363
DO YOU HEAR ME?


01:00:35.364 --> 01:00:38.199
YOU GOTTA LEAVE THAT HOUSE.


01:00:38.200 --> 01:00:40.868
HE'S COMING BACK
TO AVENGE HIS MOTHER.


01:00:40.869 --> 01:00:42.836
YOU HEAR ME?


01:00:42.837 --> 01:00:44.105
HUH?


01:00:44.106 --> 01:00:46.307
[shouting]
YOU HEAR ME?


01:00:46.308 --> 01:00:49.076
HE'LL KILL YOU ALL!
YOU HEAR ME?


01:00:49.077 --> 01:00:50.077
- AH!


01:00:50.078 --> 01:00:51.678
- JESUS.


01:00:51.679 --> 01:00:53.114
YOU OKAY?


01:00:53.115 --> 01:00:56.183
- YES, JUST SOME SERIOUSLY
FUCKED-UP PEOPLE IN THIS TOWN.


01:00:56.184 --> 01:01:00.087
- WHAT HAPPENED?


01:01:00.088 --> 01:01:01.322
JEN, WHAT HAPPENED?


01:01:01.323 --> 01:01:03.324
- I DON'T KNOW.
JUST, LET'S GO.


01:01:03.325 --> 01:01:06.160
I'M REALLY STARTING
TO HATE THIS PLACE.


01:01:14.036 --> 01:01:15.736
- I THINK JEN'S STARTING
TO LIKE THIS PLACE.


01:01:15.737 --> 01:01:16.971
- YEAH?
THAT'S GOOD, MAN.


01:01:16.972 --> 01:01:18.306
- HEY, WOULD YOU HAND ME
A BULB?


01:01:18.307 --> 01:01:20.007
- UH...


01:01:20.008 --> 01:01:22.076
KIND OF BUSY;
GIVE ME A SECOND.


01:01:22.077 --> 01:01:23.744
- DUDE, JUST HAND ME A BULB,
YOU HOMO.


01:01:23.745 --> 01:01:24.745
- [drops tool]


01:01:24.746 --> 01:01:25.913
DAMN IT.
DAMN IT.


01:01:25.914 --> 01:01:27.514
YOU SUCK.


01:01:27.515 --> 01:01:29.650
YOU KNOW, YOU GUYS
SHOULD REALLY THINK


01:01:29.651 --> 01:01:31.552
ABOUT REDOING ALL THE WIRING
IN HERE...


01:01:31.553 --> 01:01:35.122
I MEAN, IF YOU'RE EVER PLANNING
ON SELLING IT.


01:01:35.123 --> 01:01:36.590
- HEY, GIVE ME THE BULB.


01:01:36.591 --> 01:01:39.060
- OH, SHIT.
HERE.


01:01:39.061 --> 01:01:41.462
I STILL CAN'T BELIEVE THAT
YOU PUT THE DEED IN HER NAME.


01:01:41.463 --> 01:01:43.497
THAT'S JUST LIKE NOT GETTING HER
TO SIGN A PRE-NUP.


01:01:43.498 --> 01:01:44.498
- AHA!


01:01:44.499 --> 01:01:45.499
smack


01:01:45.500 --> 01:01:46.834
- OH.


01:01:46.835 --> 01:01:49.670
DUDE.


01:01:49.671 --> 01:01:50.704
- THANKS, BRO.


01:01:50.705 --> 01:01:51.705
- I'LL GO CHECK THE BOX.


01:01:51.706 --> 01:01:52.940
- YEAH, PLEASE DO.


01:01:52.941 --> 01:01:55.009
- [growling]


01:01:55.010 --> 01:01:57.878
[metal scraping]


01:02:01.950 --> 01:02:02.950
- WHERE IS IT?


01:02:02.951 --> 01:02:03.951
DID IT WORK?


01:02:03.952 --> 01:02:04.952
- DID YOU FLIP IT?


01:02:04.953 --> 01:02:05.987
- YEAH. FLIPPED IT.


01:02:05.988 --> 01:02:07.521
- LOOKS LIKE THE WIRES
ARE CROSSED.


01:02:07.522 --> 01:02:08.990
PROBABLY SOMEWHERE
IN THE BASEMENT.


01:02:08.991 --> 01:02:10.657
SEE HOW IT RUNS DOWN?


01:02:10.658 --> 01:02:13.160
I'LL GO CHECK IT OUT.


01:02:13.161 --> 01:02:14.661
- IF YOU'RE NOT BACK IN A WEEK,


01:02:14.662 --> 01:02:15.662
I'LL DRAG THE LAKE.


01:02:15.663 --> 01:02:17.498
- YEAH, ALL RIGHT.


01:02:17.499 --> 01:02:20.667
- AND STAY OUT OF THAT WINE!


01:02:20.668 --> 01:02:23.670
[eerie music]


01:02:23.671 --> 01:02:31.612
¶ ¶


01:02:50.265 --> 01:02:52.299
- HELLO?


01:03:15.057 --> 01:03:17.558
HOLY SHIT.


01:03:21.629 --> 01:03:23.898
FUCK ME.


01:03:23.899 --> 01:03:25.365
OH.


01:03:25.366 --> 01:03:27.767
EVAN'S GONNA FLIP HIS SHIT.


01:03:27.768 --> 01:03:29.669
YO, "E"!


01:03:31.772 --> 01:03:33.840
OH, MY GOD.


01:03:43.918 --> 01:03:46.753
- [grumbles]


01:03:46.754 --> 01:03:47.754
- [laughs nervously]


01:03:47.755 --> 01:03:48.855
OH, SHIT.


01:03:48.856 --> 01:03:51.992
OH, DUDE, THAT WAS--
YOU SCARED ME.


01:03:51.993 --> 01:03:53.560
ALL RIGHT, YOU GOT ME.


01:03:53.561 --> 01:03:57.097
WE'RE EVEN.


01:03:57.098 --> 01:03:59.966
UGH!


01:03:59.967 --> 01:04:01.001
- HEY, MIKE!


01:04:01.002 --> 01:04:02.769
I TOLD YOU STAY AWAY
FROM MY WINE.


01:04:02.770 --> 01:04:04.505
- [moaning]


01:04:04.506 --> 01:04:07.907
- FRIGGIN' DRUNK.


01:04:07.908 --> 01:04:10.110
- YOU FUCKER!


01:04:10.111 --> 01:04:12.346
FUCK!


01:04:12.347 --> 01:04:13.547
NO!


01:04:13.548 --> 01:04:17.484
[moaning]


01:04:31.799 --> 01:04:34.834
- MIKE.


01:04:34.835 --> 01:04:37.404
GOD DAMN IT.


01:04:41.476 --> 01:04:44.878
MIKE!


01:04:44.879 --> 01:04:47.648
MIKE!


01:04:47.649 --> 01:04:49.716
SWEAR TO GOD, IF YOU THROW
THAT SCARECROW AT ME AGAIN,


01:04:49.717 --> 01:04:55.455
I'M GONNA PUNCH YOU
IN THE SAC.


01:04:55.456 --> 01:04:56.690
COME ON, MIKE.


01:04:56.691 --> 01:04:59.426
IT'S NOT FUNNY ANYMORE.
WE GOT STUFF TO DO.


01:05:06.401 --> 01:05:08.502
YOU GOT THE DOOR OPEN, HUH?


01:05:08.503 --> 01:05:09.936
WHERE'D YOU FIND THE KEY?


01:05:09.937 --> 01:05:13.039
MIKE?
WHERE ARE YOU?


01:05:15.076 --> 01:05:18.978
HEY, I SEE YOU, DIPSHIT.


01:05:18.979 --> 01:05:22.649
ALL RIGHT, ENJOY THE SMELL.
I'M LOCKING YOU IN.


01:05:33.160 --> 01:05:34.828
WHAT'S UP WITH YOUR FACE?


01:05:34.829 --> 01:05:37.764
- [grumbling]


01:05:46.307 --> 01:05:48.908
- [screams]


01:05:51.846 --> 01:05:54.381
HEY! HELP!


01:05:54.382 --> 01:05:55.749
AH!


01:05:55.750 --> 01:05:57.451
SOMEBODY HELP ME!


01:06:04.425 --> 01:06:07.427
[tense percussive music]


01:06:07.428 --> 01:06:15.369
¶ ¶


01:06:24.679 --> 01:06:28.948
[breathing heavily]


01:06:28.949 --> 01:06:30.216
- [growling]


01:06:36.424 --> 01:06:37.457
crack!


01:06:39.294 --> 01:06:40.294
crack!


01:06:40.295 --> 01:06:43.397
UGH!


01:06:43.398 --> 01:06:47.334
- AH!


01:06:47.335 --> 01:06:49.068
UGH!


01:06:49.069 --> 01:06:52.071
[dramatic music]


01:06:52.072 --> 01:07:00.013
¶ ¶


01:07:38.285 --> 01:07:43.256
¶ ¶


01:07:43.257 --> 01:07:46.493
- OH!


01:07:46.494 --> 01:07:48.294
OH!


01:08:00.941 --> 01:08:04.110
- WHO'S THE CREEPER?


01:08:04.111 --> 01:08:06.380
- IT'S OKAY.
I KNOW HIM.


01:08:06.381 --> 01:08:07.381
- YEAH?
- YEAH.


01:08:07.382 --> 01:08:08.682
COULD YOU PULL THE CAR AROUND?


01:08:08.683 --> 01:08:09.783
- YEAH.


01:08:09.784 --> 01:08:11.251
HEY, SCREAM IF YOU NEED ME,
ALL RIGHT?


01:08:11.252 --> 01:08:15.355
- YEAH, I'LL MEET YOU INSIDE.


01:08:15.356 --> 01:08:16.857
- I DON'T MEAN TO BOTHER YOU,


01:08:16.858 --> 01:08:20.627
BUT YOU HAVEN'T SEEN MR. PECK
OUT HERE TODAY, HAVE YOU?


01:08:20.628 --> 01:08:23.229
- ACTUALLY, I JUST LEFT HIM
DOWN AT THE STORE.


01:08:23.230 --> 01:08:27.768
HE--HE WAS REALLY DRUNK
AND ACTING PRETTY STRANGE.


01:08:27.769 --> 01:08:29.035
- IT'S THIS PLACE.


01:08:29.036 --> 01:08:31.605
IT DREDGES UP A LOT
OF REALLY BAD MEMORIES FOR HIM.


01:08:31.606 --> 01:08:34.875
- YEAH, HE TOLD ME...
EVERYTHING.


01:08:36.911 --> 01:08:38.678
- EVAN?


01:08:42.750 --> 01:08:44.584
MIKE?


01:08:54.662 --> 01:08:58.231
HELLO?


01:08:58.232 --> 01:09:01.234
[ominous music]


01:09:01.235 --> 01:09:08.975
¶ ¶


01:09:10.044 --> 01:09:13.647
[laughing]


01:09:13.648 --> 01:09:16.983
"FOR YOU."


01:09:16.984 --> 01:09:19.553
IT LOOKS LIKE A KINDERGARTENER
WROTE IT.


01:09:19.554 --> 01:09:24.390
[water running]


01:09:24.391 --> 01:09:26.993
MIKE?


01:09:26.994 --> 01:09:29.563
MIKE?


01:09:29.564 --> 01:09:33.366
COME OUT, COME OUT,
WHEREVER YOU ARE.


01:09:40.240 --> 01:09:42.308
- IF YOU DO SEE HIM,


01:09:42.309 --> 01:09:43.710
YOU'LL GIVE ME A CALL, RIGHT?


01:09:43.711 --> 01:09:45.712
- OKAY.
I'LL DO THAT.


01:09:45.713 --> 01:09:48.682
- GOOD.


01:09:48.683 --> 01:09:50.383
- HEY, FRED.


01:09:50.384 --> 01:09:52.452
WHAT IS MR. PECK SO AFRAID OF?


01:09:56.724 --> 01:10:00.159
- THE PAST.


01:10:09.771 --> 01:10:12.773
[eerie music]


01:10:12.774 --> 01:10:20.714
¶ ¶


01:10:26.788 --> 01:10:28.155
crash!


01:10:36.230 --> 01:10:39.566
[water running]


01:10:55.717 --> 01:10:58.919
- [sighing]


01:11:10.664 --> 01:11:14.167
[door opens]


01:11:14.168 --> 01:11:17.170
[ominous music]


01:11:17.171 --> 01:11:25.112
¶ ¶


01:11:49.536 --> 01:11:50.871
[screams]


01:11:56.644 --> 01:11:59.045
- ANNETTE.


01:11:59.046 --> 01:12:02.348
YOU UP HERE?


01:12:11.826 --> 01:12:15.328
ANNETTE!


01:12:15.329 --> 01:12:16.897
AH!


01:12:21.869 --> 01:12:25.038
[crying]


01:12:25.039 --> 01:12:28.041
[foreboding music]


01:12:28.042 --> 01:12:35.982
¶ ¶


01:13:03.544 --> 01:13:06.880
- [coughing]


01:13:09.951 --> 01:13:17.891
¶ ¶


01:13:19.327 --> 01:13:23.263
- [crying]


01:13:47.654 --> 01:13:50.656
[ominous music]


01:13:50.657 --> 01:13:55.328
¶ ¶


01:13:55.329 --> 01:13:58.865
[screaming]


01:13:58.866 --> 01:14:01.801
[crying]


01:14:16.217 --> 01:14:24.157
¶ ¶


01:14:26.994 --> 01:14:29.796
OH!


01:14:29.797 --> 01:14:33.233
[grunting]


01:14:33.234 --> 01:14:41.174
¶ ¶


01:14:47.714 --> 01:14:48.714
crack!


01:14:48.715 --> 01:14:51.684
AH!


01:14:51.685 --> 01:14:57.257
¶ ¶


01:14:57.258 --> 01:14:58.258
[footsteps]


01:14:58.259 --> 01:14:59.692
SHIT.


01:15:18.346 --> 01:15:20.347
- OH, THE DEVIL.


01:15:24.418 --> 01:15:26.552
THE DEVIL!


01:15:38.699 --> 01:15:40.867
- AH!


01:15:53.947 --> 01:15:56.616
[door opens]


01:15:56.617 --> 01:15:59.619
[foreboding music]


01:15:59.620 --> 01:16:07.560
¶ ¶


01:16:28.282 --> 01:16:36.222
¶ ¶


01:16:52.673 --> 01:16:55.075
- [groaning]


01:17:02.149 --> 01:17:04.217
[engine turns over]


01:17:27.841 --> 01:17:30.577
NOT THIS TIME, ASSHOLE.


01:17:35.649 --> 01:17:38.651
[dramatic orchestral music]


01:17:38.652 --> 01:17:46.593
¶ ¶


01:17:52.799 --> 01:17:55.602
[car horn honking]


01:18:03.344 --> 01:18:05.745
I'M RIGHT HERE, ASSHOLE!


01:18:05.746 --> 01:18:09.315
- [crying]


01:18:09.316 --> 01:18:12.352
- [moaning]


01:18:12.353 --> 01:18:14.820
- EVAN. EVAN.
HONEY.


01:18:14.821 --> 01:18:17.357
[crying]


01:18:17.358 --> 01:18:20.393
OKAY, COME ON.
WE'LL GET YOU OUT OF HERE.


01:18:23.930 --> 01:18:26.199
OKAY, I GOT YOU, BABY.


01:18:26.200 --> 01:18:27.200
BABY.


01:18:27.201 --> 01:18:29.001
[crying]


01:18:29.002 --> 01:18:30.936
[door closes]


01:18:46.220 --> 01:18:49.222
[gentle piano music]


01:18:49.223 --> 01:18:57.163
¶ ¶


01:19:01.035 --> 01:19:03.269
thud!


01:19:03.270 --> 01:19:06.305
[whimpers]


01:19:06.306 --> 01:19:08.974
- COME ON, LEONARD!


01:19:08.975 --> 01:19:11.310
COME ON, YOU SACK OF SHIT!


01:19:14.714 --> 01:19:17.616
[brains squishing]


01:19:23.090 --> 01:19:28.261
SICK SON OF A BITCH!


01:19:28.262 --> 01:19:31.264
[ominous music]


01:19:31.265 --> 01:19:39.205
¶ ¶


01:19:43.444 --> 01:19:47.346
- I'M SENDING YOU BACK TO HELL,
MOTHERFUCKER.


01:19:47.347 --> 01:19:49.782
[horn blaring]
- COME ON!


01:19:51.918 --> 01:19:53.586
SON OF A BITCH.


01:19:53.587 --> 01:19:55.154
HUH?


01:19:55.155 --> 01:19:57.890
YOU'RE ONE SICK
SON OF A BITCH!


01:19:59.393 --> 01:20:01.026
I KILLED YOU ONCE.


01:20:01.027 --> 01:20:02.528
I CAN DO IT AG--


01:20:06.200 --> 01:20:07.700
AGH!


01:20:07.701 --> 01:20:11.504
[tense percussive music]


01:20:11.505 --> 01:20:13.306
THAT'S THE BEST--
THE BEST YOU CAN DO?


01:20:13.307 --> 01:20:14.873
OKAY, BOY.


01:20:14.874 --> 01:20:17.110
[coughing]


01:20:21.115 --> 01:20:22.281
[laughing]


01:20:22.282 --> 01:20:23.816
THAT'S A PRETTY NEW FACE
YOU GOT THERE.


01:20:23.817 --> 01:20:26.819
OH, YOU'RE BEAUTIFUL,
YOU FUCK FACE!


01:20:26.820 --> 01:20:28.821
OOH!
WOW!


01:20:28.822 --> 01:20:30.055
YOU'RE AFRAID OF ME,
IS THAT IT?


01:20:30.056 --> 01:20:31.757
WELL, I AIN'T AFRAID OF YOU.


01:20:31.758 --> 01:20:33.292
I AIN'T AFRAID OF NOTHING.


01:20:33.293 --> 01:20:41.234
¶ ¶


01:20:44.171 --> 01:20:45.804
COME ON.
FUCKING FREAK!


01:20:45.805 --> 01:20:47.240
HUH?
COME ON.


01:20:47.241 --> 01:20:48.241
COME ON!


01:20:48.242 --> 01:20:50.709
COME ON, TRY TO KILL ME.


01:20:52.779 --> 01:20:55.014
OOH!


01:20:57.951 --> 01:21:05.891
¶ ¶


01:21:17.103 --> 01:21:20.640
- LEONARD!


01:21:20.641 --> 01:21:24.410
LET HIM GO.


01:21:24.411 --> 01:21:26.279
- [grumbling]


01:21:26.280 --> 01:21:28.914
- YES.


01:21:28.915 --> 01:21:32.351
JUST LET HIM GO, OKAY?


01:21:32.352 --> 01:21:34.753
THERE YOU GO, BABY.


01:21:39.493 --> 01:21:43.329
- I'M SO PROUD OF YOU.


01:21:45.499 --> 01:21:47.400
- [whimpering]


01:21:48.502 --> 01:21:51.504
[dramatic music]


01:21:51.505 --> 01:21:59.445
¶ ¶


01:22:02.649 --> 01:22:04.217
- UGH!


01:22:09.289 --> 01:22:12.592
- I DID IT--THE 3-YEAR-OLD.
I DID FOR THE BABY.


01:22:12.593 --> 01:22:13.726
I KILLED HIM.


01:22:13.727 --> 01:22:15.561
- YEAH, YOU DID.


01:22:15.562 --> 01:22:16.962
YOU DID.


01:22:16.963 --> 01:22:18.864
LOOK, WE'RE GOING TO GET YOU
AN AMBULANCE, OKAY?


01:22:18.865 --> 01:22:22.435
- YOU HAVE TO BURN HIM.


01:22:22.436 --> 01:22:26.305
BURN...HIM.


01:22:30.510 --> 01:22:33.512
[dramatic music]


01:22:33.513 --> 01:22:37.082
¶ ¶


01:22:37.083 --> 01:22:39.285
- WOW!


01:22:42.723 --> 01:22:48.561
¶ ¶


01:22:48.562 --> 01:22:51.731
- WAIT!


01:23:03.977 --> 01:23:06.445
WHAT EXACTLY HAPPENED HERE?


01:23:06.446 --> 01:23:08.213
- YEAH, FRED FROM
THE GENERAL STORE CALLED US


01:23:08.214 --> 01:23:09.515
AFTER MR. PECK WENT MISSING.


01:23:09.516 --> 01:23:11.183
WE STUMBLED UPON THIS MESS.


01:23:11.184 --> 01:23:14.487
WE'RE STILL TRYING TO PIECE IT
TOGETHER.


01:23:14.488 --> 01:23:17.290
SHE'S A LITTLE SHAKEN UP,
AS YOU MIGHT TELL.


01:23:17.291 --> 01:23:18.857
JENNIFER.


01:23:18.858 --> 01:23:20.626
JEN, I WANT TO SPEAK TO YOU
FOR A MINUTE.


01:23:20.627 --> 01:23:23.596
- HI, JENNIFER.
MY NAME IS ARTHUR BROWN.


01:23:23.597 --> 01:23:26.031
I'M REALLY SORRY.


01:23:26.032 --> 01:23:30.235
THIS MUST BE REALLY HORRIBLE
FOR YOU.


01:23:30.236 --> 01:23:32.004
I SPOKE TO EVAN ON THE PHONE
YESTERDAY,


01:23:32.005 --> 01:23:33.539
AND HE ASKED ME
IF I'D COME OUT.


01:23:33.540 --> 01:23:35.240
I WOULD APPRAISE THE ANTIQUES
IN THE HOUSE,


01:23:35.241 --> 01:23:37.009
AND I CAN TELL YOU


01:23:37.010 --> 01:23:40.546
THAT YOU ARE SITTING ON OVER
A MILLION DOLLARS IN ASSETS.


01:23:40.547 --> 01:23:43.882
NOW, I DON'T EXPECT YOU
TO ANSWER ME RIGHT AWAY,


01:23:43.883 --> 01:23:46.452
BUT I WOULD LIKE TO EXTEND
THE OFFER.


01:23:51.157 --> 01:23:52.558
- I'M SORRY.


01:23:52.559 --> 01:23:56.495
- NO, I'M SORRY.


01:23:56.496 --> 01:23:58.297
I LOOK FORWARD
TO HEARING FROM YOU.


01:23:58.298 --> 01:23:59.598
- THANK YOU.


01:23:59.599 --> 01:24:00.933
- THANK YOU, SIR.
- APPRECIATE IT.


01:24:00.934 --> 01:24:04.737
THANKS A LOT.


01:24:04.738 --> 01:24:06.339
YOU CAN GO NOW
IF YOU WANT TO.


01:24:06.340 --> 01:24:08.341
GOT YOU A HOTEL ROOM
OUT THERE AT THE INTERSTATE.


01:24:08.342 --> 01:24:09.608
STAY AS LONG AS YOU WANT.


01:24:09.609 --> 01:24:11.143
THE COUNTY WILL TAKE CARE
OF YOU.


01:24:11.144 --> 01:24:12.945
I CAN GET ONE OF MY OFFICERS
TO KEEP YOU COMPANY


01:24:12.946 --> 01:24:17.082
TILL YOUR PARENTS GET HERE.


01:24:17.083 --> 01:24:19.218
ALL RIGHT, THEN.


01:24:19.219 --> 01:24:24.223
HEY, HOLD HIM UP.


01:24:24.224 --> 01:24:25.424
SHOOT.


01:24:25.425 --> 01:24:28.160
GET THIS SORRY SON OF A BITCH
IN A BODY BAG.


01:24:32.499 --> 01:24:35.501
[tranquil orchestral music]


01:24:35.502 --> 01:24:43.442
¶ ¶


01:25:10.203 --> 01:25:15.140
- [weeping]


01:25:49.042 --> 01:25:52.044
[ominous music]


01:25:52.045 --> 01:25:59.985
¶ ¶


01:26:04.491 --> 01:26:05.624
[screams]


01:26:05.625 --> 01:26:08.627
[heavy metal music]


01:26:08.628 --> 01:26:16.569
¶ ¶

